/* pl — 원고: ~/Documents/Study/서재_원고/pl.py 에서 생성(한/영 동시). 직접 고치지 말고 원고를 고친다. */
export const sections = [{"id": "guide", "title": "문서 안내", "sub": "0장", "part": "시작", "html": "<header class=\"g-cover\"><div class=\"g-kicker\">학습서 · 데이터 엔지니어링</div><h1>실시간 데이터 파이프라인</h1><p class=\"g-lead\">사건이 생기면 몇 초 안에 정리된 숫자로 바꾸는 길을, 정의·이유·동작 원리·실패 케이스·코드·AI에게 시키는 법까지 한 틀로 익혀요.</p><div class=\"g-chips\"><span class=\"g-chip\">중학생도 읽는 설명</span><span class=\"g-chip\">숫자 예시</span><span class=\"g-chip\">실패 케이스</span><span class=\"g-chip\">한/영</span></div></header><div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-guide\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">00</span>문서 안내</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>이 책은 실시간 데이터 파이프라인을 처음 접하는 사람이 「무엇이고, 왜 필요하고, 어디서 어떻게 깨지는가」를 같은 틀로 익히도록 쓴 학습서다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>도구 이름만 외우면 숫자가 조용히 틀려도 알아채지 못한다. 실시간 데이터의 사고는 에러 없이 일어난다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.1 목적과 범위</h4><p>대상은 데이터를 다뤄 본 비개발자와 초급 개발자다. 범위는 「사건이 생김 → 전달 → 가공 → 저장 → 조회 → 운영」 전 구간이다.</p><p>모든 장은 같은 가상 쇼핑몰(주문·결제) 하나를 예시로 쓴다. 숫자는 설명용 예시 값이며 실제 제품의 측정값이 아니다.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.2 장의 구조</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>순서</th><th>요소</th><th>무엇을 답하나</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>정의</td><td>한 문장으로 무엇인가</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td>이게 없으면</td><td>왜 필요한가</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>동작 원리</td><td>그림 한 장과 숫자 예시</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>단계 카드</td><td>입력·출력·담당·실패를 눌러서 펼침</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td>실패 케이스</td><td>어디서 어떻게 깨지는가</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td>코드 · 키워드</td><td>심화. AI에게 시킬 때 넣을 말</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td>다루지 않는 것</td><td>경계를 숨기지 않는다</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.3 표기</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>배지</th><th>뜻</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-ok\">실습으로 확인 가능</span></td><td>로컬에서 가짜 데이터로 직접 돌려 확인할 수 있다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">개념만 다룸</span></td><td>개념과 판단 기준만 다룬다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">상황에 따라 다름</span></td><td>팀·상황에 따라 답이 달라진다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></td><td>이 책에서 다루지 않는다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">심화</span></td><td>코드가 나오는 심화 구간</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.4 기준 시점</h4><p>2026-10-15 기준이다. 제품 버전은 자주 바뀌므로 설정 이름과 동작은 공식 문서(12장 근거 자료)로 다시 확인한다. 이 책은 버전 고유 값보다 개념과 판단 기준을 다룬다.</p></section></div>"}, {"id": "overview", "title": "이벤트 한 건의 여행", "sub": "1장", "part": "기초", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-overview\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">01</span>이벤트 한 건의 여행</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>실시간 데이터 파이프라인은 사건이 생긴 뒤 몇 초 안에 그 사건을 정리된 숫자로 바꿔 조회할 수 있게 하는, 끊기지 않는 처리 경로다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>어제까지의 숫자만 본다. 오늘 오후 2시의 문제는 내일 아침에야 알게 된다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.1 배치와 실시간</h4><p>배치는 아침에 배달되는 종이 신문이고, 실시간은 스포츠 생중계다. 둘은 우열이 아니라 「늦으면 손해인가」로 고른다.</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>구분</th><th>배치</th><th>실시간</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">처리 단위</td><td>하루·한 시간 치 묶음</td><td>사건 한 건씩 계속</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">지연</td><td>분~일</td><td>초~분</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">틀렸을 때</td><td>다시 돌리면 끝</td><td>이미 나간 결과가 틀릴 수 있어 재계산 설계 필요</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">운영 부담</td><td>낮음</td><td>항상 켜 둬야 해서 높음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">적합한 업무</td><td>월 보고서, 주간 분석</td><td>품절 표시, 부정 결제 차단, 현장 대시보드</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.2 동작 원리 — 주문 A-1001 한 건</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 126\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"이벤트 한 건의 경로\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">주문 앱</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">버튼 클릭</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">주문 DB</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">행 저장</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">CDC</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">변경 읽기</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">보관·전달</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Flink</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">가공·집계</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">저장소</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Iceberg</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">각 칸은 이 책의 한 장이다: 6장 CDC → 2장 Kafka → 4·5장 Flink → 7장 저장소</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 1-1</b> 이벤트 한 건이 화면 속 숫자가 되기까지</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>예시 시각</th><th>어디에서</th><th>데이터의 모양</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.000</td><td>주문 앱 → 주문 DB</td><td><code>{id: A-1001, status: CREATED, amount: 42000}</code></td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.300</td><td>CDC가 DB 변경 기록을 읽음</td><td><code>{event_id: e-001, op: c, occurred_at: 10:01:00}</code></td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.350</td><td>Kafka orders 토픽</td><td>파티션 2, offset 1841 (예시)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:01.200</td><td>Flink</td><td>10:01~10:02 칸 합계에 +42,000</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:02:10</td><td>Flink → StarRocks</td><td>워터마크가 칸을 닫은 뒤 1분 매출 확정(허용 지연 10초 가정)</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">읽는 법</b>주문은 10:01:00에 생겼지만 「1분 매출」은 10:02:10에야 확정된다. 빠름과 정확함은 맞바꾸는 관계이고, 그 다이얼이 4장의 워터마크다.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.3 누가 무엇을 책임지나</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>구성요소</th><th>책임</th><th>책임이 아닌 것</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">CDC (Debezium)</td><td>DB 변경을 이벤트로 바꿔 내보냄</td><td>이벤트 가공·집계</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Kafka</td><td>순서 있게 보관하고 여러 곳에 전달</td><td>합계·조인 같은 계산</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink</td><td>연속 계산, 시간 처리, 상태 기억</td><td>장기 보관</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">StarRocks</td><td>지금 상태·최근 집계의 빠른 조회</td><td>모든 이력의 영구 보관</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Iceberg</td><td>모든 변경 이력의 보관과 재계산 원본</td><td>초 단위 대시보드 응답</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">헷갈림 주의</b>Kafka는 계산하지 않는다. 합계를 내는 쪽은 Flink다.</div></section></div>"}, {"id": "kafka", "title": "Kafka", "sub": "2장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-kafka\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">02</span>Kafka — 이벤트를 잃지 않고 전달하는 장부</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>Kafka는 이벤트를 토픽에 시간 순서로 덧붙여 보관하고, 읽는 쪽이 각자 「어디까지 읽었는지(오프셋)」를 기억하며 가져가게 하는 분산 로그다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>보내는 쪽과 받는 쪽이 직접 연결되어, 받는 쪽이 잠깐 멈추면 그동안의 데이터가 사라지거나 보내는 쪽까지 멈춘다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.1 동작 원리</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 212\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"토픽·파티션·컨슈머 그룹\"><text x=\"46\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-ts2\">오프셋 0 → 오래된 것부터 오른쪽으로 쌓임</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"56\" class=\"g-t\">P0</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1002</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1004</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1002</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1007</text><path d=\"M232,51 L372,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"114\" class=\"g-t\">P1</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1005</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1005</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1006</text><path d=\"M186,109 L372,109\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"172\" class=\"g-t\">P2</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1003</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><path d=\"M232,167 L372,167\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"470\" y=\"36\" width=\"130\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">C1</text><text x=\"535\" y=\"75\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">P0, P1 읽음</text><rect x=\"470\" y=\"126\" width=\"130\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">C2</text><text x=\"535\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">P2 읽음</text><path d=\"M372,51 L468,61\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M372,109 L468,70\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M372,167 L468,151\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">컨슈머 그룹 sales-dashboard</text><text x=\"660\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"g-ts2\" style=\"display:none\"></text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 2-1</b> 같은 주문(1001)은 항상 같은 파티션 P2에 쌓여 순서가 보존된다. 컨슈머 그룹 안에서 파티션 하나는 한 번에 한 소비자만 읽는다.</figcaption></figure><p>토픽은 파티션이라는 여러 줄로 나뉜다. 순서는 <b>한 파티션 안에서만</b> 보장된다. 그래서 「같은 주문의 사건은 같은 줄로」 보내려고 주문 ID를 키로 쓴다.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.2 숫자 예시</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>키(주문)</th><th>이벤트</th><th>파티션 · 오프셋 (예시)</th><th>결과</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">A-1001</td><td>CREATED → PAID → SHIPPED</td><td>P2 · 1841, 1842, 1843</td><td>순서 보존</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">A-1002</td><td>CREATED → CANCELED</td><td>P0 · 2210, 2211</td><td>순서 보존</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">키 없음</td><td>CREATED, PAID</td><td>P1 · 77 / P2 · 1850 (갈라짐)</td><td>PAID가 먼저 처리될 수 있음</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>파티션 3개일 때 소비자 수</th><th>배정</th><th>효과</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>C1: P0, P1, P2</td><td>병렬성 1</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>C1: P0 · C2: P1 · C3: P2</td><td>최대 병렬성</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>C4는 배정 없음(대기)</td><td>늘려도 빨라지지 않음 — 파티션 수가 병렬성의 상한</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.3 단계 카드</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 발행(produce)</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">보내는 쪽이 토픽에 이벤트를 쓴다</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>이벤트 본문 + 키(주문 ID)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>파티션과 오프셋이 붙은 기록</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>보내는 앱</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>재시도 중 같은 이벤트가 두 번 쓰일 수 있다 → 멱등 프로듀서로 막는다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 보관(retain)</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">읽혔는지와 무관하게 정해진 기간 보관</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>발행된 기록</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>재읽기 가능한 로그</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Kafka 브로커</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>복제본이 없으면 브로커 장애 때 유실. 보관 기간이 지나면 다시 읽을 수 없다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 소비(consume)</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">읽는 쪽이 자기 위치부터 가져간다</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>컨슈머 그룹 + 마지막 커밋 오프셋</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>이벤트 묶음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>받는 앱(Flink 등)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>소비자가 죽으면 파티션이 다른 소비자에게 옮겨진다(재조정). 이때 일부를 다시 읽을 수 있다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ 커밋(commit)</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">「여기까지 처리했다」 책갈피를 꽂는다</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>처리를 끝낸 오프셋</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>그룹의 새 읽기 위치</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>받는 앱</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>처리 전에 커밋하면 죽었을 때 유실, 처리 후에 커밋하면 죽었을 때 중복</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.4 전달 보장</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>보장</th><th>커밋 시점</th><th>죽으면</th><th>쓰는 곳</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">at-most-once</td><td>처리 전</td><td>유실 가능</td><td>로그 샘플링처럼 일부 빠져도 되는 곳</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">at-least-once</td><td>처리 후</td><td>중복 가능</td><td>대부분. 중복을 이벤트 ID로 거른다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">exactly-once</td><td>트랜잭션·멱등 결합</td><td>중복·유실 없음(조건부)</td><td>금액 합계. 5장에서 조건을 본다</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.5 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">합계가 두 번 더해짐</td><td>재시도·재조정으로 같은 이벤트 재전달</td><td>event_id 로 중복 제거</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">이벤트가 영영 처리 안 됨</td><td>처리 전에 커밋</td><td>처리 → 저장 → 커밋 순서</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">취소가 결제보다 먼저 처리됨</td><td>키 없이 보내 파티션이 갈라짐</td><td>주문 ID를 키로</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">한 소비자만 바쁨</td><td>특정 키에 트래픽이 쏠림(hot key)</td><td>키 설계 변경·분산 키</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">파티션을 늘렸더니 순서가 깨짐</td><td>키→파티션 매핑이 바뀜</td><td>처음에 여유 있게 정하고 변경은 계획해서</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.6 코드 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">심화</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">보내는 쪽</p><pre><code> 1  from confluent_kafka import Producer\n 2  import json\n 3  \n 4  producer = Producer({\n 5      \"bootstrap.servers\": \"localhost:9092\",\n 6      \"enable.idempotence\": True,\n 7  })\n 8  \n 9  order = {\"event_id\": \"e-001\", \"order_id\": \"A-1001\",\n10           \"amount\": 42000, \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-14T10:01:00+09:00\"}\n11  \n12  producer.produce(\"order-events\", key=order[\"order_id\"],\n13                   value=json.dumps(order))\n14  producer.flush()</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>Kafka 라이브러리를 가져온다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–7</td><td>서버 주소와 <b>enable.idempotence</b>(재전송해도 한 번만 저장) 설정</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9–10</td><td>이벤트 한 건. <b>event_id</b>는 중복 거르기용, <b>occurred_at</b>은 사건 발생 시각</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12–13</td><td><b>key=주문 ID</b>라 같은 주문은 같은 파티션으로 간다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">14</td><td>모아 둔 것을 모두 보낼 때까지 기다린다</td></tr></table></div><p class=\"g-small\">받는 쪽</p><pre><code> 1  from confluent_kafka import Consumer\n 2  import json\n 3  \n 4  consumer = Consumer({\n 5      \"bootstrap.servers\": \"localhost:9092\",\n 6      \"group.id\": \"sales-dashboard\",\n 7      \"auto.offset.reset\": \"earliest\",\n 8      \"enable.auto.commit\": False,\n 9  })\n10  consumer.subscribe([\"order-events\"])\n11  \n12  seen = set()\n13  while True:\n14      msg = consumer.poll(1.0)\n15      if msg is None or msg.error():\n16          continue\n17      event = json.loads(msg.value())\n18      if event[\"event_id\"] not in seen:\n19          seen.add(event[\"event_id\"])\n20          print(\"sales +\", event[\"amount\"])\n21      consumer.commit(msg)</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–9</td><td><b>group.id</b>는 같은 팀 이름, <b>earliest</b>는 책갈피가 없으면 처음부터</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td><b>auto commit 끄기</b> — 처리 후에만 직접 커밋</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12–20</td><td>1초마다 가져와 이미 본 event_id는 건너뛴다(운영에서는 메모리 대신 DB·Flink 상태에 보관)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">21</td><td>처리가 끝난 뒤에 커밋</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.7 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>소비자를 파티션 수보다 늘리면 왜 안 빨라지나?</summary><div>파티션 하나는 같은 그룹에서 한 번에 한 소비자에게만 배정된다. 남는 소비자는 일이 없다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>주문 ID를 키로 쓰는 이유와 대가는?</summary><div>같은 주문의 순서를 보존하기 위해서다. 대신 특정 주문·고객에 트래픽이 몰리면(hot key) 한 파티션이 병목이 된다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>커밋을 처리 전에 하면 무슨 일이 생기나?</summary><div>처리 중 죽으면 그 이벤트는 이미 읽은 것으로 기록돼 다시 오지 않는다 → 유실.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.8 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>복제 인수·ISR 설정의 세부 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>SASL·ACL 같은 보안 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>압축(compaction) 토픽 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">개념만 다룸</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "contract", "title": "이벤트 계약", "sub": "3장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-contract\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">03</span>이벤트 계약 — 모양을 바꿔도 되는 규칙</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>이벤트 계약은 이벤트에 어떤 필드가 있고 각 필드가 무슨 뜻·형식인지, 그리고 그 모양을 어떻게 바꿔도 되는지를 보내는 쪽과 받는 쪽이 함께 지키는 약속이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>보내는 쪽이 필드 이름 하나를 바꾸면 받는 쪽은 에러 없이 빈 값을 읽고, 합계가 조용히 틀린다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.1 최소 계약</h4><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"event_id\": \"e-001\",\n 3    \"event_type\": \"ORDER_CREATED\",\n 4    \"aggregate_id\": \"A-1001\",\n 5    \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-14T10:01:00+09:00\",\n 6    \"schema_version\": 1,\n 7    \"payload\": { \"amount\": 42000, \"currency\": \"KRW\", \"status\": \"CREATED\" }\n 8  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td><b>event_id</b> — 전역에서 유일. 중복 제거 열쇠</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td><b>aggregate_id</b> — 이 이벤트가 속한 업무 대상(주문). Kafka 키로 쓴다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td><b>occurred_at</b> — 사건이 일어난 시각(이벤트 시간). 시간대 포함</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td><b>schema_version</b> — 모양이 바뀔 때 읽는 쪽이 분기</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td><b>payload</b> — 업무 내용. 금액은 단위(원)와 통화를 같이 적는다</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.2 호환성 세 가지</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>종류</th><th>뜻</th><th>먼저 배포할 쪽</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">backward</td><td>새 모양으로 옛 이벤트를 읽을 수 있다</td><td>받는 쪽(소비자)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">forward</td><td>옛 모양의 읽는 쪽이 새 이벤트를 읽을 수 있다</td><td>보내는 쪽(생산자)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">full</td><td>둘 다</td><td>순서 상관없음</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.3 변경 판정표</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>변경</th><th>안전한가</th><th>이유</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">선택 필드 추가(기본값 있음)</td><td>안전</td><td>옛 읽는 쪽은 모르는 필드를 무시, 새 읽는 쪽은 기본값 사용</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">필수 필드 추가(기본값 없음)</td><td>위험</td><td>새 모양으로 옛 이벤트를 읽을 때 채울 값이 없다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">필드 삭제</td><td>조건부</td><td>옛 읽는 쪽이 그 필드를 필수로 기대하면 깨진다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">타입 변경</td><td>대개 위험</td><td>정수→문자열은 읽기 실패. 확장 변환(int→long)만 허용되는 경우가 있다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">이름 변경</td><td>위험</td><td>삭제 + 추가로 보인다. 별칭(alias)이나 이행 기간이 필요</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">호환성 검사가 못 잡는 것</b>「원」을 「천원」으로 바꾸는 변경은 타입이 같아 검사를 통과한다. 의미는 계약 문서에 단위로 못 박는다.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.4 이름을 바꾸는 안전한 절차</h4><ol><li>새 필드를 <b>추가</b>하고 보내는 쪽이 옛·새 필드를 둘 다 쓴다</li><li>받는 쪽을 새 필드로 전환한다</li><li>옛 필드를 읽는 곳이 없음을 확인한다(로그·검사)</li><li>옛 필드 쓰기를 멈추고 계약에서 제거한다</li></ol></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.5 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>필수 필드를 추가하면 왜 위험한가?</summary><div>이미 쌓인 옛 이벤트에는 그 값이 없어, 새 모양으로 읽을 때 채울 수 없다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>이름 변경이 「삭제 + 추가」인 이유는?</summary><div>도구는 이름으로 필드를 식별하므로 옛 이름은 사라지고 새 이름이 생긴 것으로 본다.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.6 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>Avro·Protobuf 문법 세부 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>레지스트리 운영·권한 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "time", "title": "시간과 윈도우", "sub": "4장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-time\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">04</span>시간과 윈도우 — 「언제」를 기준으로 합친다</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>이벤트 시간은 사건이 실제로 일어난 시각, 처리 시간은 시스템이 그 사건을 본 시각이다. 워터마크는 「이 시각 이전 사건은 거의 다 도착했다」고 선언하는 선이고, 윈도우는 시간을 일정한 칸으로 자르는 방법이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>도착 시각으로 집계하면 지하철에서 늦게 전송된 주문이 엉뚱한 칸의 매출에 들어가, 같은 데이터인데 보고서마다 숫자가 다르다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.1 동작 원리</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 214\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"이벤트 시간과 도착 시간\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" class=\"g-ts2\">일어난 시각</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"150\" class=\"g-ts2\">도착한 시각</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"60\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:00</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:02</text><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:04</text><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"442\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:06</text><line x1=\"442\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"442\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"442\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"442\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"566\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:08</text><line x1=\"566\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"566\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"566\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"566\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"690\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:10</text><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"184\" class=\"g-flh g-fd\"/><text x=\"322\" y=\"26\" class=\"g-th\" style=\"font-size:12px\">창 경계 10:05</text><path d=\"M142,60 L143,150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><circle cx=\"143\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><path d=\"M370,60 L371,150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><circle cx=\"370\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><circle cx=\"371\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><path d=\"M375,60 L463,150\" class=\"g-flh\"/><circle cx=\"375\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-th\"/><circle cx=\"463\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-th\"/><text x=\"143\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">e1</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">e2 · e3</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-th\" style=\"font-size:12px\">e3 · 85초 늦게 도착</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 4-1</b> e3은 10:04:55에 일어났지만 10:06:20에 도착했다. 창 경계(10:05)가 그 사이에 끼어 있다.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>이벤트</th><th>일어난 시각</th><th>도착 시각</th><th>금액</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e1</td><td>10:01:10</td><td>10:01:11</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e2</td><td>10:04:50</td><td>10:04:51</td><td>20,000</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e3</td><td>10:04:55</td><td>10:06:20</td><td>30,000</td></tr></table></div><p>5분 칸 10:00~10:05의 매출을 설정별로 계산하면 다음과 같다(그 사이 다른 주문이 계속 들어와 워터마크가 앞으로 간다고 가정).</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>설정</th><th>10:00~10:05 칸 합계</th><th>칸이 확정되는 시점</th><th>해석</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">도착 시각 기준</td><td>30,000</td><td>10:05:00</td><td>e3이 다음 칸(10:05~10:10)으로 밀려 틀린 칸에 들어감</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">이벤트 시간 + 워터마크 10초</td><td>30,000</td><td>10:05:10</td><td>e3은 늦은 이벤트(late)라 기본 설정에서 버려짐</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">이벤트 시간 + 허용 지연 120초</td><td>60,000</td><td>10:07:00</td><td>e3까지 포함하지만 확정이 2분 늦음</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">핵심</b>늦은 이벤트를 얼마나 기다릴지는 기술이 아니라 <b>업무가 정하는</b> 값이다. 정확성과 지연 사이의 다이얼이다.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.2 단계 카드</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 시간 기준 정하기</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">무엇을 「시각」으로 볼지</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>이벤트의 occurred_at</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>모든 집계가 쓰는 시각 필드</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>계약(3장)과 Flink 테이블 정의</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>시간대가 섞이면 9시간 어긋난 칸에 들어간다(UTC vs KST)</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 워터마크 정하기</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">얼마나 늦은 것까지 기다릴지</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>실측한 도착 지연 분포</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>허용 지연(예: 10초)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>업무 담당자 + 데이터 엔지니어</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>너무 짧으면 정상 지연이 late로 버려지고, 너무 길면 결과 확정이 늦다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 늦은 이벤트 처리</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">버릴지, 기다릴지, 따로 모을지</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>워터마크를 넘겨 도착한 이벤트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>버림 / 허용 지연 / 사이드 출력(별도 저장)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Flink 작업 설계</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>조용히 버리면 합계가 모자란다. 최소한 개수를 센다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ 창 종류 고르기</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">칸의 모양</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>질문 (분당 매출? 최근 5분? 방문 한 번?)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>tumbling / sliding / session</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>요구사항</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>sliding은 같은 이벤트가 여러 칸에 들어가 계산량이 늘어난다</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.3 창 종류</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>종류</th><th>모양</th><th>예</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">tumbling</td><td>겹치지 않는 고정 칸</td><td>분당 매출</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">sliding</td><td>겹치며 밀려가는 칸</td><td>최근 5분 이동 평균(1분마다 갱신)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">session</td><td>활동이 끊기면 닫히는 칸</td><td>한 손님의 방문 구간</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.4 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">결과가 영영 안 나옴</td><td>한 파티션에 이벤트가 없어 워터마크가 멈춤</td><td>유휴 시간 제한(idle timeout) 설정</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">새벽에 숫자가 모자람</td><td>늦은 이벤트를 조용히 버림</td><td>late 개수 지표로 감시</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">기기마다 시각이 다름</td><td>클라이언트 시계 오차</td><td>서버 수신 시각을 보조 필드로 함께 기록</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9시간 어긋남</td><td>UTC/KST 혼용</td><td>계약에 시간대 포함 형식 고정</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.5 코드 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">심화</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">Flink SQL</p><pre><code> 1  CREATE TABLE orders (\n 2    order_id    STRING,\n 3    amount      DECIMAL(12, 0),\n 4    occurred_at TIMESTAMP(3),\n 5    WATERMARK FOR occurred_at AS occurred_at - INTERVAL '10' SECOND\n 6  ) WITH (\n 7    'connector' = 'kafka',\n 8    'topic' = 'order-events',\n 9    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = 'kafka:9092',\n10    'format' = 'json',\n11    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset'\n12  );\n13  \n14  SELECT window_start, window_end, SUM(amount) AS sales\n15  FROM TABLE(\n16    TUMBLE(TABLE orders, DESCRIPTOR(occurred_at), INTERVAL '5' MINUTE))\n17  GROUP BY window_start, window_end;</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1–5</td><td>Kafka 토픽을 끝없이 늘어나는 표로 정의. <b>WATERMARK</b>는 「10초 늦은 것까지 기다린다」</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6–12</td><td>이 표의 원천이 order-events 토픽이고 처음부터(earliest) 읽는다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">14–17</td><td><b>TUMBLE</b> — 겹치지 않는 5분 칸으로 자르기. 기준은 occurred_at(이벤트 시간)</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.6 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>워터마크를 길게 하면 무엇을 얻고 무엇을 잃나?</summary><div>늦은 이벤트를 더 받아 정확해지지만, 결과가 확정되는 시점이 늦어진다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>왜 처리 시간이 아닌 이벤트 시간으로 집계하나?</summary><div>네트워크 지연·재시도가 있어도 같은 데이터면 같은 결과가 나오기 때문이다(재현 가능).</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.7 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>윈도우 조인·패턴 감지(CEP) <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>Flink DataStream API 세부 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "state", "title": "상태와 복구", "sub": "5장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-state\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">05</span>상태와 복구 — 죽어도 숫자가 맞는 이유</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>상태는 연속 처리가 계산 도중 기억하는 값(합계, 이미 본 ID)이고, 체크포인트는 그 상태와 읽은 위치를 일정 간격으로 함께 저장한 세이브 지점이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>서버가 한 번 죽을 때마다 합계가 사라지거나 처음부터 다시 계산해야 하고, 다시 읽다가 같은 건을 두 번 더한다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.1 동작 원리</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 144\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"체크포인트와 복구\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">읽기</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Kafka offset</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">상태 갱신</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">합계 += 금액</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">체크포인트</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">30초마다 저장</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">장애</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">서버 종료</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">복원</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">마지막 저장본</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">재처리</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">저장 이후만</text><path d=\"M666,90 C666,132 54,132 54,92\" class=\"g-fla g-fd\" marker-end=\"url(#g-aha)\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">복원 후 offset 부터 다시 읽는다</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 5-1</b> 상태와 읽기 위치를 <b>같이</b> 저장하기 때문에, 복원하면 「합계」와 「어디까지 읽었나」가 서로 맞는다.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>예시 시각</th><th>일</th><th>합계</th><th>읽은 위치(P0)</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:00</td><td>체크포인트 cp-7 저장</td><td>1,250,000</td><td>900</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:20</td><td>계속 처리</td><td>1,310,000</td><td>940</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:25</td><td>서버 종료</td><td>(메모리 사라짐)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:40</td><td>cp-7 로 복원</td><td>1,250,000</td><td>900</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:41~</td><td>900~940 의 40건을 다시 읽어 재계산</td><td>1,310,000</td><td>940</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">읽는 법</b>40건을 다시 읽었지만 합계는 두 번 더해지지 않는다. 복원된 합계(1,250,000)에서 다시 시작하기 때문이다.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.2 「정확히 한 번」의 뜻</h4><p>Flink의 exactly-once는 「이벤트가 물리적으로 한 번만 처리된다」가 아니라 「복구 뒤에도 <b>Flink가 관리하는 상태</b>에 한 번만 반영된다」는 결과 의미다. 외부 저장소까지 한 번만 쓰려면 조건이 더 필요하다.</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>소스</th><th>싱크</th><th>종단 간 결과</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">다시 읽을 수 있음(Kafka)</td><td>트랜잭션 또는 멱등 쓰기</td><td>정확히 한 번 반영</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">다시 읽을 수 있음</td><td>그냥 INSERT</td><td>복구 구간 결과가 두 번 쓰일 수 있음(중복)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">다시 읽을 수 없음</td><td>무엇이든</td><td>유실 가능</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.3 체크포인트와 세이브포인트</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>구분</th><th>체크포인트</th><th>세이브포인트</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">목적</td><td>장애 자동 복구</td><td>업그레이드·이관·롤백</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">누가 만드나</td><td>시스템이 주기적으로</td><td>사람이 명시적으로</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">수명</td><td>시스템이 관리(오래된 것 삭제)</td><td>사람이 지울 때까지 유지</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.4 단계 카드 — 장애 한 번의 처리</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 저장</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">주기적으로 상태+위치를 함께 저장</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>연산 상태, 소스 offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>체크포인트 파일</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Flink</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>연속 실패하면 복구 지점이 점점 옛것이 된다 → 알림 대상</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 감지</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">작업자(TaskManager) 종료를 알아챔</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>하트비트 끊김</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>작업 중단·재시작 결정</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Flink + Kubernetes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>재시작이 반복(루프)되면 원인(코드·설정)을 먼저 고친다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 복원</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">마지막 성공 체크포인트에서 상태 복구</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>체크포인트 위치</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>합계·읽기 위치 복구</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Flink</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>코드 변경으로 상태 모양이 달라지면 복원 실패 → 세이브포인트로 호환 확인</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ 재처리·검증</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">저장 이후 구간을 다시 읽고 숫자를 대조</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>offset 이후 이벤트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>복구 전후 같은 합계·고유 건수</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>운영자</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>싱크가 멱등이 아니면 복구 구간 결과가 중복된다</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.5 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">복구 뒤 합계가 두 배</td><td>비멱등 싱크</td><td>기본키 upsert 또는 트랜잭션 싱크</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">상태가 계속 커짐</td><td>중복 제거용 ID를 영원히 보관</td><td>보존 기간(TTL) 설정</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">체크포인트가 자주 실패</td><td>싱크·상태가 느려서 시간 초과</td><td>체크포인트 소요시간 지표 감시</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">배포 후 복원 실패</td><td>상태 모양 비호환</td><td>세이브포인트로 사전 검증</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.6 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>왜 상태와 읽기 위치를 같이 저장하나?</summary><div>따로 저장하면 복원 뒤 합계와 위치가 어긋나 일부를 빠뜨리거나 두 번 센다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>exactly-once인데 DB에 중복이 생기는 이유는?</summary><div>Flink 상태에만 해당하는 보장이고, 싱크가 멱등·트랜잭션이 아니면 재시도가 두 번 반영된다.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.7 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>상태 백엔드(RocksDB) 튜닝 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>고가용성(HA) 구성 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">개념만 다룸</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "cdc", "title": "CDC와 outbox", "sub": "6장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-cdc\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">06</span>CDC와 outbox — DB 변화를 빠짐없이 이벤트로</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>CDC는 DB가 스스로 적는 변경 기록(트랜잭션 로그)을 읽어 행이 바뀐 사실을 이벤트로 내보내는 방법이다. outbox는 업무 데이터와 「이 이벤트를 보내겠다」는 기록을 한 트랜잭션에 함께 저장하는 패턴이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>앱이 DB와 Kafka에 각각 쓰면 한쪽만 성공하는 순간이 생기고, 그 틈에 빠진 주문은 영영 맞지 않는다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.1 동작 원리 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">심화</span></h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 190\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"이중 쓰기와 CDC 비교\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-t\">이중 쓰기 (위험)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">주문 앱</text><path d=\"M112,50 L200,40\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M112,68 L200,108\" class=\"g-flh\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"202\" y=\"24\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">DB 저장 ✔</text><rect x=\"202\" y=\"92\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka 실패 ✘</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">DB에는 있고 Kafka에는 없는 주문</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-t\">CDC / outbox (안전)</text><rect x=\"400\" y=\"34\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">주문 앱</text><path d=\"M502,59 L528,59\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"530\" y=\"34\" width=\"90\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"575\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">DB</text><text x=\"575\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">+ outbox</text><path d=\"M622,59 L648,59\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"650\" y=\"34\" width=\"62\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"681\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">CDC</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"112\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">한 트랜잭션에 업무 행 + 발행 의도 저장</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"130\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CDC가 커밋된 것만 읽어 Kafka로</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 6-1</b> 이중 쓰기는 두 곳에 따로 쓰는 틈이 있고, CDC·outbox는 DB에 확정된 것만 따라 읽는다.</figcaption></figure><p>DB는 모든 변경을 먼저 로그에 적는다(PostgreSQL의 WAL). Debezium 같은 CDC 도구는 이 로그를 읽어 「주문 A-1001이 CREATED에서 PAID로 바뀜」 같은 이벤트를 만든다.</p><p class=\"g-small\">Debezium 변경 이벤트(예시)</p><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"op\": \"u\",\n 3    \"before\": { \"id\": \"A-1001\", \"status\": \"CREATED\", \"amount\": 42000 },\n 4    \"after\":  { \"id\": \"A-1001\", \"status\": \"PAID\",    \"amount\": 42000 },\n 5    \"source\": { \"lsn\": 33100248, \"ts_ms\": 1760403667000 }\n 6  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td><b>op</b> — c(생성) u(수정) d(삭제) r(처음 스냅샷)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3–4</td><td><b>before/after</b> — 바뀌기 전·후 행. 무엇이 바뀌었는지 비교한다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td><b>lsn</b> — 로그 위치. 같은 변경이 두 번 오면 이 값으로 걸러낸다</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.2 단계 카드</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 초기 스냅샷</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">지금까지의 행을 먼저 모두 이벤트로</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>대상 표의 현재 행</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>op=r 이벤트 묶음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Debezium</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>큰 표는 오래 걸리고 DB에 부하를 준다 → 한가한 시간에</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 증분 전환</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">스냅샷 시점 이후 변경만 이어 읽기</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>스냅샷 시점의 로그 위치</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>op=c/u/d 이벤트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Debezium</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>전환 구간에 같은 행이 두 번 올 수 있다 → 중복 제거</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 장애 후 재개</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">저장해 둔 로그 위치부터 다시 읽기</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>마지막 offset(LSN)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>끊긴 지점 이후의 이벤트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Kafka Connect</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>복제 슬롯이 로그를 계속 붙잡아 DB 디스크가 찰 수 있다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ 스키마 변경</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">열이 추가·삭제될 때</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>DDL 변경</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>새 모양의 이벤트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>DB 관리자 + 3장 계약</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>받는 쪽이 새 열을 모르면 무시하거나 실패 — 호환성 규칙을 따른다</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.3 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">DB 디스크가 계속 참</td><td>복제 슬롯이 로그를 붙잡음(커넥터 중단)</td><td>슬롯 지연 모니터링, 안 쓰는 슬롯 삭제</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">삭제가 안 반영됨</td><td>op=d 를 소비자가 처리하지 않음</td><td>삭제 정책(소프트/하드)을 계약에 명시</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">같은 변경이 두 번 옴</td><td>CDC는 at-least-once</td><td>key + lsn 으로 중복 제거</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">큰 트랜잭션에서 지연 급증</td><td>커밋 전까지 이벤트가 안 나감</td><td>대량 변경은 나눠서 커밋</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.4 코드 — 커넥터 설정 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">심화</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">Debezium 설정</p><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"name\": \"shop-orders-cdc\",\n 3    \"config\": {\n 4      \"connector.class\": \"io.debezium.connector.postgresql.PostgresConnector\",\n 5      \"database.hostname\": \"postgres\",\n 6      \"database.dbname\": \"shop\",\n 7      \"database.user\": \"cdc_reader\",\n 8      \"database.password\": \"${file:/secrets/cdc.properties:password}\",\n 9      \"plugin.name\": \"pgoutput\",\n10      \"topic.prefix\": \"shop\",\n11      \"table.include.list\": \"public.orders,public.payments\"\n12    }\n13  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>줄</th><th>이 줄이 하는 일</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>PostgreSQL용 CDC 커넥터</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5–7</td><td>어느 DB를 볼지. 읽기 전용 계정을 쓴다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td>비밀번호는 코드에 쓰지 않고 파일·비밀 저장소에서 읽는다</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9</td><td>PostgreSQL 기본 변경 읽기 방식</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10–11</td><td><b>topic.prefix</b>는 토픽 이름 앞머리, <b>table.include.list</b>는 따라 읽을 표</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.5 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>CDC가 이중 쓰기보다 안전한 이유는?</summary><div>DB에 커밋된 변경만 읽으므로 「DB엔 있고 Kafka엔 없는」 틈이 줄어든다. outbox를 쓰면 발행 의도까지 같은 트랜잭션에 묶인다.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>CDC 이벤트가 중복될 수 있는 이유는?</summary><div>장애 후 재개 때 마지막 저장 위치 이후를 다시 읽기 때문이다(at-least-once).</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.6 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>PostgreSQL 외 DB(MySQL·Oracle) <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li><li>Debezium 서버(Kafka Connect 없는) 모드 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "store", "title": "저장과 조회", "sub": "7장", "part": "핵심 원리", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-store\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">07</span>저장과 조회 — 「지금」과 「그때」를 나눠 담기</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>실시간 조회용 저장소(StarRocks 같은 분석 DB)는 「지금 상태·최근 집계」를 빠르게 답하고, 테이블 포맷 저장소(Iceberg)는 「모든 변경 이력」을 싸게 오래 보관해 과거 시점으로 다시 계산하게 한다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>하나로 다 하려 하면 조회가 느리거나, 틀린 숫자를 고칠 원본이 없다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.1 질문이 저장소를 정한다</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 126\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"저장소 역할 분리\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">Flink</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">정리된 결과</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">지금 상태</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">빠른 조회</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"605\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">대시보드·API</text><text x=\"605\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">초 단위 응답</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Flink는 같은 결과를 Iceberg에도 쓴다. 잘못된 숫자가 나오면 Iceberg의 원본에서 다시 계산해 StarRocks를 덮어쓴다.</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 7-1</b> 한 번 계산한 결과를 두 곳에 나눠 담는다</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>질문</th><th>알맞은 곳</th><th>이유</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">지금 주문 A-1001의 상태는?</td><td>StarRocks</td><td>최신 값을 키로 바로 조회(upsert)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">대시보드 첫 화면이 1초 안에 떠야 한다</td><td>StarRocks</td><td>분석용 열 저장·병렬 처리</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">어제 오후 2시 시점의 주문 상태는?</td><td>Iceberg</td><td>스냅샷으로 과거 시점 조회(time travel)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">지난달 집계를 다른 기준으로 다시 계산</td><td>Iceberg</td><td>원본 이력이 모두 남아 있음</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.2 비교</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>항목</th><th>StarRocks</th><th>Iceberg</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">역할</td><td>빠른 조회용 데이터베이스</td><td>저장 형식(테이블 포맷)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">강점</td><td>낮은 지연의 집계·조회</td><td>이력 보관, 스냅샷, 여러 엔진에서 읽기</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">약점</td><td>모든 이력을 오래 두면 비용↑</td><td>초 단위 대시보드에는 느림</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">운영 주의</td><td>키·파티션 설계가 성능을 좌우</td><td>작은 파일이 쌓이면 합치기(compaction) 필요</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.3 단계 카드</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 적재</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">같은 결과를 두 곳에 쓴다</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>Flink 출력(기본키 포함)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>StarRocks 행, Iceberg 스냅샷</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>Flink 커넥터</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>한쪽만 성공하면 두 저장소 숫자가 갈라진다 → ②에서 대조</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 대조</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">두 저장소의 건수·금액 합계 비교</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>같은 구간의 두 저장소 값</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>차이 0 또는 차이 보고</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>운영자 / 자동 점검</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>차이가 나면 원본(Iceberg)을 기준으로 삼는다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 재처리</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">원본에서 다시 계산해 덮어쓰기</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>Iceberg 원본, 고친 계산 규칙</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>StarRocks의 새 결과</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>데이터 엔지니어</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>덮어쓰는 동안 조회가 섞이지 않게 새 표로 만든 뒤 교체한다</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.4 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">같은 주문이 두 행</td><td>기본키 설계 오류</td><td>업무 ID(order_id)를 키로</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Iceberg 조회가 점점 느려짐</td><td>작은 파일이 쌓임</td><td>주기적 compaction</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">두 저장소 숫자가 다름</td><td>한쪽 적재 지연·실패</td><td>②단계 대조를 자동화</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.5 확인 문제</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>「지금 상태」와 「어제 2시 상태」를 각각 어디에 묻나?</summary><div>지금은 StarRocks, 어제 2시는 Iceberg 스냅샷이다.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.6 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>다른 분석 DB(ClickHouse 등)와의 비교 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">상황에 따라 다름</span></li><li>카탈로그·권한 관리 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "ops", "title": "운영 기준", "sub": "8장", "part": "운영", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-ops\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">08</span>운영 기준 — 「성공」 로그 하나로 끝내지 않기</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>운영 기준은 「프로그램이 돌고 있다」가 아니라 「숫자가 맞고 제때 도착한다」를 지표로 상시 확인하겠다는 약속이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>처리는 성공 로그를 내는데 합계는 틀리거나 여섯 시간 늦은 상태를, 사용자가 먼저 발견한다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.1 무엇을 보나</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>층</th><th>지표</th><th>이상 신호</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Kafka</td><td>컨슈머 lag, 처리율</td><td>lag 이 계속 증가, 특정 파티션만 편중</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink</td><td>백프레셔, 체크포인트 소요·실패, 재시작 횟수</td><td>체크포인트 연속 실패, 재시작 반복</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">데이터</td><td>입력/출력 건수, 고유 키 수, 금액 합계, null 비율, DLQ</td><td>시스템은 정상인데 업무 수치가 불일치</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">저장소</td><td>반영 지연, 거부된 행, 최신 시각</td><td>적재 성공률 저하, 최신 시각 정체</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">사용자</td><td>화면에 보이는 최신 데이터 시각</td><td>파이프라인 정상인데 조회는 오래됨</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.2 목표 예시 (SLO)</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>지표</th><th>학습용 목표</th><th>검증 방법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">종단 간 지연 p95</td><td>10초 이하</td><td>occurred_at 과 조회 반영 시각 차이</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">유실</td><td>0건</td><td>원천 event_id 와 Iceberg 대조</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">업무 중복</td><td>0건</td><td>같은 event_id 를 3번 보내 금액이 한 번만 반영되는지</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">복구 시간</td><td>5분 이하</td><td>작업자 강제 종료부터 처리율 회복까지</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.3 장애 대응 순서</h4><details class=\"g-stage\" open><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① 영향 좁히기</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">어떤 화면·시간 구간이 틀렸나</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>사용자 신고·알림</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>영향받은 소비자·시간 구간</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>온콜</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>범위를 모르면 복구가 과하거나 모자란다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② 흐름 따라 병목 찾기</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">원천 → Kafka lag → Flink 백프레셔 → 싱크</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>층별 지표(8.1)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>막힌 지점</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>온콜</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>소비자만 늘리면 안 풀리는 경우가 많다(파티션 상한, 느린 싱크)</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ 정합성 판단</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">유실·중복 가능성과 자동 재시작의 안전성</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>건수·합계 대조</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>「그냥 재시작 가능」 또는 「중지 후 복구」</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>온콜 + 업무 담당</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>틀린 숫자가 계속 나가면 먼저 출력을 멈추는 편이 낫다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ 복구·검증</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">안전한 저장점에서 복원, 숫자 대조</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>마지막 안전 체크포인트/세이브포인트, offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>시스템 지표와 업무 수치가 모두 정상</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>온콜</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>시스템 지표만 보고 끝내지 않는다</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">⑤ 재발 방지</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">경고를 사람 기억이 아니라 자동 검사로</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">입력</td><td>사후 기록</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">출력</td><td>새 알림·가드·테스트</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">담당</td><td>팀</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실패하면</td><td>「조심하자」로 끝나면 같은 일이 반복된다</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.4 배포·롤백 체크리스트</h4><ul class=\"g-checklist\"><li>입력 계약의 깨지는 변경을 CI에서 검사한다</li><li>되돌릴 저장점(세이브포인트) 위치를 기록한다</li><li>신·구 버전이 동시에 읽고 써도 되는지 확인한다</li><li>별도 컨슈머 그룹으로 실제 입력 일부를 먼저 검증한다</li><li>입력 건수·업무 합계·최신 시각을 구버전과 대조한다</li><li>롤백 명령과 재처리 시작 offset을 적어 둔다</li></ul></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.5 실패 케이스</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>증상</th><th>원인</th><th>막는 법</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">알림이 너무 많아 무시됨</td><td>임계값 없이 모든 지표를 알림</td><td>사용자 영향 지표(지연·불일치)만 호출 대상으로</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">로그는 성공인데 숫자가 틀림</td><td>업무 수치를 안 봄</td><td>건수·합계 대조를 지표로</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.6 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>온콜 조직·당직 체계 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">상황에 따라 다름</span></li><li>비용 최적화 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "build", "title": "만들어 보기", "sub": "9장", "part": "실습", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-build\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">09</span>만들어 보기 — 가상 주문·결제 파이프라인</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>캡스톤은 가상 주문·결제 데이터로 이 책의 모든 장을 직접 돌려 보고, 각 장의 주장을 숫자로 확인하는 실습이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>읽기만 하면 「알았다」와 「만들 수 있다」 사이의 간극이 남는다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.1 만들 것</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 104\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"캡스톤 구조\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Postgres</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">orders</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">payments</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Debezium</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">CDC</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">계약 검사</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Flink</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">조인·중복 제거</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Iceberg</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">현재 / 이력</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">관측</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">lag·DLQ</text></svg><figcaption><b>그림 9-1</b> 주문·결제 상태가 바뀌면 10초 안에 대시보드에 보이고, 장애·재시작에도 금액이 중복되지 않는다</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>성공 기준</th><th>목표</th><th>검증</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">종단 간 지연 p95</td><td>≤ 10s</td><td>발생 시각 vs 조회 반영 시각</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">유실</td><td>0</td><td>원천 대비 Iceberg 건수</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">업무 중복</td><td>0</td><td>같은 event_id 3회 발행</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">복구 시간</td><td>≤ 5 min</td><td>작업자 강제 종료 실험</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">계약 안전성</td><td>깨지는 변경 100% 차단</td><td>호환성 테스트 CI</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">재사용</td><td>두 번째 파이프라인은 설정만 추가</td><td>shipment 파이프라인 생성</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">안전 수칙</b>실습은 내 컴퓨터(docker compose)와 가짜 데이터만 쓴다. 회사 서버·실데이터는 쓰지 않는다.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.2 12주 로드맵</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>주</th><th>주제</th><th>완료 기준</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">0</td><td>기준선: 구조를 아는 말로 그려 보기</td><td>20분 안에 초안, 모르는 항목 10개 이하</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1–2</td><td>Kafka: 토픽·파티션·키·소비자 그룹 (2장)</td><td>offset을 바꿔 같은 이벤트를 다시 읽고 순서 보장 범위를 로그로 설명</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>이벤트 계약 (3장)</td><td>호환/비호환 변경을 CI에서 구분</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–5</td><td>Flink SQL, 이벤트 시간·워터마크 (4장)</td><td>같은 입력을 두 기준으로 계산해 차이를 증명</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td>상태·체크포인트·재시작 (5장)</td><td>복구 전후 고유 건수·금액 동일</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td>Postgres CDC (6장)</td><td>변경 이력이 빠짐없이 순서대로, DELETE 정책 문서화</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td>저장소 연결 (7장)</td><td>「지금」과 「어제 시점」을 각 저장소에서 답함</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9–10</td><td>Kubernetes 운영, 관측·SLO (8장)</td><td>싱크 장애 2분 뒤 알림이 몇 분 내 오는지 증거</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">11</td><td>설정 기반 표준화</td><td>두 번째 파이프라인을 코드 복사 없이 생성</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12</td><td>캡스톤 방어</td><td>아래 질문 12개 이상을 그림·실측값으로 답함</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.3 역량 판정</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>수준</th><th>판정</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">설명 가능</td><td>이 책의 확인 문제를 문서 없이 설명</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">구축 가능</td><td>캡스톤의 정상 흐름을 처음부터 재현</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">운영 가능</td><td>장애 실험 6개를 복구하고 숫자로 대조</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">플랫폼화 가능</td><td>설정·SQL만으로 두 번째 파이프라인</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">주도 가능</td><td>요구사항에서 SLO·계약·키·보장·저장소·롤백 기준을 먼저 질문</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.4 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>실데이터·실서버 연동 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">상황에 따라 다름</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "vibe", "title": "AI에게 시키는 법", "sub": "10장", "part": "심화", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-vibe\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">10</span>AI에게 시키는 법 — 아는 말을 넣으면 덜 헤맨다</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>바이브코딩은 AI에게 말로 코드를 시키는 작업이고, 이 장의 키워드는 AI가 「돌아가는 데모」가 아니라 「틀리지 않는 코드」를 쓰게 만드는 제약 조건이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>제약을 말하지 않으면 AI는 가장 흔한 예제를 준다. 흔한 예제는 중복·유실·순서를 보호하지 않는다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.1 키워드 사전</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>키워드</th><th>뜻</th><th>넣으면 달라지는 것</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">partition key = order_id</td><td>같은 주문은 같은 줄로</td><td>순서가 섞이는 코드를 피함</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">idempotent producer / event_id dedup</td><td>중복 방지</td><td>재시도해도 두 번 더해지지 않음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">manual offset commit after processing</td><td>처리 후 책갈피</td><td>유실 없는 소비 루프</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">event time + watermark (10s)</td><td>사건 시각 기준 집계</td><td>늦은 데이터를 빠뜨리지 않음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">tumbling window 1 minute</td><td>1분 칸 집계</td><td>집계 단위를 정확히</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">checkpoint / exactly-once sink</td><td>세이브·한 번만 반영</td><td>재시작해도 숫자 유지</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">DLQ (dead letter queue)</td><td>망가진 이벤트 보관함</td><td>에러 이벤트를 버리지 않고 모음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">schema registry, backward compatible</td><td>이벤트 모양 약속</td><td>필드 변경 시 받는 쪽 보호</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">docker compose, local only, fake data</td><td>로컬·가짜 데이터</td><td>회사 서버를 건드리지 않음</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.2 같은 부탁, 다른 결과</h4><div class=\"g-grid2\"><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">헤매는 프롬프트</b><br>Kafka로 주문 데이터 실시간으로 보내는 코드 짜줘</div><div class=\"g-key g-okkey\"><b class=\"g-l\">덜 헤매는 프롬프트</b><br>Python confluent-kafka로 order-events 토픽 프로듀서를 짜 줘. key는 order_id, idempotent producer 켜고, 이벤트에 event_id·occurred_at(ISO8601) 포함. 컨슈머는 group.id=sales-dashboard, 처리 후 수동 offset commit, event_id로 중복 제거. docker compose로 로컬 Kafka 하나만 띄우고 가짜 주문 100건으로 테스트하는 방법까지.</div></div><p class=\"g-small\">왜 다른가: 키·중복·책갈피 규칙을 먼저 정해 주면 AI가 「일단 돌아가는」 코드 대신 「틀리지 않는」 코드를 쓴다.</p><div class=\"g-grid2\"><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">헤매는 프롬프트</b><br>Flink로 1분 매출 집계해줘</div><div class=\"g-key g-okkey\"><b class=\"g-l\">덜 헤매는 프롬프트</b><br>Flink SQL로 Kafka order-events를 읽어 occurred_at 기준 1분 tumbling window 매출 합계를 내 줘. watermark는 10초 지연 허용. 형식이 틀린 행은 DLQ 토픽으로 보내고, 결과는 콘솔에 출력. 처리 시간이 아니라 이벤트 시간 기준인 이유를 주석으로.</div></div><p class=\"g-small\">왜 다른가: 「무슨 시간 기준인지」를 안 정하면 AI는 보통 처리 시간으로 짜서 늦은 주문이 빠진다.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.3 프롬프트 틀</h4><ol><li><b>무엇을</b>: 한 줄 목표 (예: 1분 매출)</li><li><b>입력·출력</b>: 토픽 이름, 이벤트 필드</li><li><b>보장</b>: 중복 없음 / 유실 없음 / 순서 범위</li><li><b>시간</b>: 기준(이벤트 시간)과 허용 지연</li><li><b>환경</b>: 로컬, docker compose, 가짜 데이터</li><li><b>검증</b>: 어떤 실험으로 맞는지 보일 것(예: 같은 이벤트 3번)</li></ol></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.4 AI가 준 코드, 이것만 확인</h4><ul class=\"g-checklist\"><li>키를 주문 ID 같은 업무 ID로 잡았나?</li><li>offset commit이 처리 <b>뒤</b>에 있나?</li><li>중복을 거르는 event_id 가 있나?</li><li>집계가 이벤트 시간 기준인가?</li><li>비밀번호가 코드에 박혀 있지 않나?</li><li>실습이 로컬·가짜 데이터인가?</li></ul></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.5 다루지 않는 것</h4><ul><li>특정 AI 도구별 사용법 <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "limits", "title": "다루지 않는 것과 선택 기준", "sub": "11장", "part": "경계", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-limits\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">11</span>다루지 않는 것과 선택 기준</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>이 장은 이 책이 의도적으로 다루지 않은 것과, 정답이 상황에 따라 달라지는 선택을 숨기지 않고 모아 둔 목록이다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>경계를 숨기면 「책에 없으니 필요 없다」로 읽혀, 운영에서 가장 먼저 빠뜨릴 것들이 빠진다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>11.1 다루지 않는 것</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>주제</th><th>상태</th><th>어디서 보나</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">보안(인증·암호화·권한)</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></td><td>각 제품의 보안 문서</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">비용 산정</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></td><td>클라우드 요금 계산기</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">멀티 리전·재해 복구</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">개념만 다룸</span></td><td>Kafka·Flink HA 문서</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">개인정보·규제 준수</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></td><td>사내 정보보호 담당</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Kafka Streams·ksqlDB 등 대안</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">이 책에서 다루지 않음</span></td><td>각 공식 문서</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>11.2 정해지지 않은 것 — 상황에 따라 다름</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>질문</th><th>판단 기준</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">직접 운영 vs 관리형 서비스</td><td>운영 인력, 장애 시 책임, 비용 (<span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">상황에 따라 다름</span>)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink vs 더 단순한 소비자 코드</td><td>상태·시간·조인이 필요한가? 아니면 소비자 앱 하나로 충분</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">실시간이 정말 필요한가</td><td>늦으면 손해인가? 아니면 배치로 충분 (1장)</td></tr></table></div></section></div>"}, {"id": "ref", "title": "용어 사전·근거·개정 이력", "sub": "12장", "part": "부록", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-ref\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">12</span>용어 사전 · 근거 자료 · 개정 이력</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">정의</b>이 장은 책 전체의 용어를 한·영 병기로 모으고, 기술 사실의 근거와 문서의 변경 이력을 남긴다.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">이게 없으면</b>용어가 흩어져 있으면 같은 말을 장마다 다르게 이해하고, 근거가 없으면 틀려도 고칠 곳을 모른다.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.1 용어 사전</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>용어</th><th>English / 한국어</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-event\">이벤트</span></td><td>「언제 무슨 일이 있었다」 한 줄 기록</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-topic\">토픽</span></td><td>이벤트를 종류별로 모아 두는 칸</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-partition\">파티션</span></td><td>토픽을 나눈 한 줄. 순서는 이 안에서만 보장</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-key\">키</span></td><td>같은 값이면 같은 파티션으로 가게 하는 값</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-offset\">오프셋</span></td><td>파티션 안 위치. 읽은 곳을 기억하는 책갈피</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-group\">컨슈머 그룹</span></td><td>같은 일을 나눠 하는 소비자 묶음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-idem\">멱등성</span></td><td>같은 요청을 여러 번 해도 결과가 한 번과 같음</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-et\">이벤트 시간</span></td><td>사건이 실제로 일어난 시각</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-pt\">처리 시간</span></td><td>시스템이 그 사건을 본 시각</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-wm\">워터마크</span></td><td>「이 시각 이전 사건은 거의 다 왔다」는 선</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-window\">윈도우</span></td><td>시간을 일정한 칸으로 자르는 방법</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-state\">상태</span></td><td>연속 처리가 기억하는 값(합계 등)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-cp\">체크포인트</span></td><td>상태+읽기 위치를 함께 저장한 자동 세이브</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-sp\">세이브포인트</span></td><td>사람이 만드는 수동 세이브(업그레이드·롤백용)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-cdc\">CDC</span></td><td>DB 변경 기록을 읽어 이벤트로 바꾸는 방법</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-outbox\">Outbox</span></td><td>업무 행과 발행 의도를 한 트랜잭션에 저장하는 패턴</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-dlq\">DLQ</span></td><td>처리 못 한 이벤트를 모아 두는 곳</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-slo\">SLO</span></td><td>지켜야 할 서비스 수준 목표(예: 지연 10초 이하)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-lag\">컨슈머 lag</span></td><td>쌓였는데 아직 못 읽은 이벤트 수</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-bp\">백프레셔</span></td><td>아래쪽이 느려서 위쪽이 밀리는 현상</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.2 근거 자료</h4><ol class=\"g-sources\"><li><a href=\"https://kafka.apache.org/quickstart/\">Apache Kafka Quickstart</a> — 토픽·producer·consumer 첫 실행</li><li><a href=\"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/concepts/time/\">Flink — Event Time & Watermarks</a> — 이벤트 시간과 워터마크</li><li><a href=\"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/learn-flink/fault_tolerance/\">Flink — Fault Tolerance</a> — 종단 간 exactly-once 조건</li><li><a href=\"https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/architecture.html\">Debezium — Architecture</a> — Kafka Connect 기반 CDC 구조</li><li><a href=\"https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/schema-registry/fundamentals/schema-evolution.html\">Schema Registry — Evolution</a> — 호환성 종류</li><li><a href=\"https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/spark-getting-started/\">Apache Iceberg — Getting Started</a> — 테이블·스냅샷</li><li><a href=\"https://docs.starrocks.io/docs/loading/Flink-connector-starrocks/\">StarRocks — Flink connector</a> — Flink에서 실시간 적재</li></ol><p>버전은 바뀌므로 실습을 시작하는 날 stable 문서를 다시 확인한다. exactly-once는 「상태에 한 번 반영」이라는 의미이며, 종단 간 보장은 재생 가능한 소스와 멱등·트랜잭션 싱크가 함께 필요하다.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.3 개정 이력</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>버전</th><th>날짜</th><th>내용</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">v0.2</td><td>2026-10-15</td><td>정의·이유·원리·단계 카드·실패 케이스·다루지 않는 것·사전의 고정 틀로 전면 재작성. 한/영 동시 제공.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">v0.1</td><td>2026-10-14</td><td>초판(개념 중심 입문, 한국어)</td></tr></table></div></section></div>"}];
export const sectionsEn = [{"id": "guide", "title": "About This Book", "sub": "Ch. 0", "part": "Start", "html": "<header class=\"g-cover\"><div class=\"g-kicker\">Study guide · Data engineering</div><h1>Real-Time Data Pipelines</h1><p class=\"g-lead\">How a business event becomes a trustworthy number within seconds — definition, reason, mechanics, failure cases, code, and how to instruct an AI — in one consistent frame.</p><div class=\"g-chips\"><span class=\"g-chip\">Plain-language</span><span class=\"g-chip\">Worked numbers</span><span class=\"g-chip\">Failure cases</span><span class=\"g-chip\">KO / EN</span></div></header><div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-guide\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">00</span>About This Book</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>This book teaches a beginner what a real-time data pipeline is, why it is needed, and where and how it breaks — using the same frame in every chapter.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>If you only memorize tool names, you will not notice when the numbers quietly go wrong. Real-time data failures rarely raise an error.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.1 Purpose and scope</h4><p>The audience is analysts and junior developers. The scope covers the whole path: event → transport → processing → storage → query → operations.</p><p>Every chapter uses the same imaginary online shop (orders and payments). Numbers are illustrative values, not benchmarks.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.2 How each chapter is laid out</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Order</th><th>Part</th><th>What it answers</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>Definition</td><td>What is it, in one sentence</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td>Without it</td><td>Why we need it</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>How it works</td><td>One diagram and a worked example</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>Stage cards</td><td>Input, output, owner, failure — tap to open</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td>Failure cases</td><td>Where and how it breaks</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td>Code and keywords</td><td>Advanced. Words to put in your AI prompt</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td>Not covered</td><td>We do not hide the edges</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.3 Notation</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Badge</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-ok\">Hands-on</span></td><td>You can run it locally with fake data</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">Concept only</span></td><td>Concepts and decision criteria only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">Depends</span></td><td>The answer depends on your team and situation</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></td><td>Out of scope for this book</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">Advanced</span></td><td>Advanced section with code</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.4 As-of date</h4><p>As of 2026-10-15. Product versions change often, so re-check setting names and behavior against the official docs (Chapter 12). This book focuses on concepts and decision criteria rather than version-specific values.</p></section></div>"}, {"id": "overview", "title": "The Journey of One Event", "sub": "Ch. 1", "part": "Basics", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-overview\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">01</span>The Journey of One Event</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>A real-time data pipeline is a continuous path that turns an event into a query-ready number within seconds of its occurrence.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>You only see numbers up to yesterday. A problem at 2 pm today is discovered tomorrow morning.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.1 Batch vs. real-time</h4><p>Batch is the morning newspaper; real-time is a live broadcast. Neither is better — choose by whether lateness costs you.</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Batch</th><th>Real-time</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Unit</td><td>A day or hour of data</td><td>One event at a time, continuously</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Latency</td><td>Minutes to days</td><td>Seconds to minutes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">When wrong</td><td>Re-run the job</td><td>Published results may be wrong; you need a recompute design</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Operations</td><td>Low</td><td>Always on, so high</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Fits</td><td>Monthly reports, weekly analysis</td><td>Out-of-stock flags, fraud blocking, live dashboards</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.2 How it works — one order, A-1001</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 126\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Path of one event\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Order app</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Click</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Order DB</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Row saved</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">CDC</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Read changes</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Store, deliver</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Flink</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Process</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Stores</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Iceberg</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Each box is a chapter: Ch.6 CDC → Ch.2 Kafka → Ch.4–5 Flink → Ch.7 stores</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 1-1</b> From one event to a number on a screen</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Time (example)</th><th>Where</th><th>Shape of the data</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.000</td><td>Order app → DB</td><td><code>{id: A-1001, status: CREATED, amount: 42000}</code></td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.300</td><td>CDC reads the DB change log</td><td><code>{event_id: e-001, op: c, occurred_at: 10:01:00}</code></td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:00.350</td><td>Kafka orders topic</td><td>partition 2, offset 1841 (example)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:01:01.200</td><td>Flink</td><td>+42,000 into the 10:01–10:02 bucket</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:02:10</td><td>Flink → StarRocks</td><td>Bucket finalized once the watermark passes it (10 s allowed lateness assumed)</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Reading it</b>The order happened at 10:01:00 but the “per-minute sales” number is final only at 10:02:10. Speed and accuracy trade off, and the dial is the watermark in Chapter 4.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>1.3 Who is responsible for what</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Component</th><th>Responsible for</th><th>Not responsible for</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">CDC (Debezium)</td><td>Turning DB changes into events</td><td>Processing or aggregating</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Kafka</td><td>Ordered storage and delivery to many readers</td><td>Calculations such as sums and joins</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink</td><td>Continuous computation, time handling, state</td><td>Long-term storage</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">StarRocks</td><td>Fast queries on current state and recent aggregates</td><td>Permanent history</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Iceberg</td><td>History archive and recompute source</td><td>Sub-second dashboards</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Common confusion</b>Kafka does not calculate. Flink produces the sums.</div></section></div>"}, {"id": "kafka", "title": "Kafka", "sub": "Ch. 2", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-kafka\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">02</span>Kafka — A Ledger That Delivers Events Without Losing Them</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>Kafka is a distributed log: it appends events to a topic in time order, and each reader remembers its own position (offset) as it consumes.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Sender and receiver are directly coupled: if the receiver pauses, data is lost during the gap or the sender stalls too.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.1 How it works</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 212\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Topic, partitions, consumer group\"><text x=\"46\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-ts2\">offset 0 → oldest first, appended to the right</text><text x=\"10\" y=\"56\" class=\"g-t\">P0</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1002</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1004</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1002</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"34\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1007</text><path d=\"M232,51 L372,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"114\" class=\"g-t\">P1</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1005</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1005</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"92\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"114\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1006</text><path d=\"M186,109 L372,109\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"10\" y=\"172\" class=\"g-t\">P2</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"66\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><rect x=\"92\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"112\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><rect x=\"138\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"158\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1003</text><rect x=\"184\" y=\"150\" width=\"40\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">1001</text><path d=\"M232,167 L372,167\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"470\" y=\"36\" width=\"130\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">C1</text><text x=\"535\" y=\"75\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">reads P0, P1</text><rect x=\"470\" y=\"126\" width=\"130\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">C2</text><text x=\"535\" y=\"165\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">reads P2</text><path d=\"M372,51 L468,61\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M372,109 L468,70\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M372,167 L468,151\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><text x=\"535\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">consumer group sales-dashboard</text><text x=\"660\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" class=\"g-ts2\" style=\"display:none\"></text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 2-1</b> Order 1001 always lands in P2, preserving its order. Within a consumer group, one partition is read by one consumer at a time.</figcaption></figure><p>A topic is split into partitions. Order is guaranteed <b>only within one partition</b>, so we use the order ID as the key to send all events of one order down the same lane.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.2 Worked example</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Key (order)</th><th>Events</th><th>Partition · offset (example)</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">A-1001</td><td>CREATED → PAID → SHIPPED</td><td>P2 · 1841, 1842, 1843</td><td>Order preserved</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">A-1002</td><td>CREATED → CANCELED</td><td>P0 · 2210, 2211</td><td>Order preserved</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">No key</td><td>CREATED, PAID</td><td>P1 · 77 / P2 · 1850 (split)</td><td>PAID may be processed first</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Consumers (3 partitions)</th><th>Assignment</th><th>Effect</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>C1: P0, P1, P2</td><td>Parallelism 1</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>C1: P0 · C2: P1 · C3: P2</td><td>Max parallelism</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>C4 gets nothing (idle)</td><td>No speed-up — partition count caps parallelism</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.3 Stage cards</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Produce</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">The sender writes an event to a topic</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Event body + key (order ID)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A record with partition and offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Producer app</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Retries may write the same event twice → prevent with an idempotent producer</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Retain</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Kept for a set period whether read or not</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Produced records</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A log that can be re-read</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Kafka brokers</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Without replicas a broker failure loses data; after retention expires you cannot re-read</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Consume</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">The reader pulls from its own position</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Consumer group + last committed offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A batch of events</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Consumer app (e.g., Flink)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>If a consumer dies its partitions move to others (rebalance); some events may be re-read</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ Commit</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Place the “processed up to here” bookmark</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>The offset you finished processing</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>The group’s new read position</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Consumer app</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Commit before processing → loss on crash; after processing → duplicates on crash</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.4 Delivery guarantees</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Guarantee</th><th>Commit timing</th><th>On crash</th><th>Use when</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">at-most-once</td><td>Before processing</td><td>May lose</td><td>Sampling, where some loss is fine</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">at-least-once</td><td>After processing</td><td>May duplicate</td><td>Most cases; dedupe by event ID</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">exactly-once</td><td>Transactions + idempotence</td><td>No loss/duplicates (conditional)</td><td>Money totals; conditions in Ch.5</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.5 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Sum counted twice</td><td>Re-delivery after retry or rebalance</td><td>Dedupe by event_id</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Event never processed</td><td>Committed before processing</td><td>Process → store → commit</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Cancel before payment</td><td>No key; partitions split</td><td>Key by order ID</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">One consumer is busy</td><td>Traffic piles on a hot key</td><td>Redesign the key or salt it</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Order broke after adding partitions</td><td>Key-to-partition mapping changed</td><td>Over-provision early; plan changes</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.6 Code <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">Advanced</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">Producer</p><pre><code> 1  from confluent_kafka import Producer\n 2  import json\n 3  \n 4  producer = Producer({\n 5      \"bootstrap.servers\": \"localhost:9092\",\n 6      \"enable.idempotence\": True,\n 7  })\n 8  \n 9  order = {\"event_id\": \"e-001\", \"order_id\": \"A-1001\",\n10           \"amount\": 42000, \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-14T10:01:00+09:00\"}\n11  \n12  producer.produce(\"order-events\", key=order[\"order_id\"],\n13                   value=json.dumps(order))\n14  producer.flush()</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1</td><td>Import the Kafka client</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–7</td><td>Server address and <b>enable.idempotence</b> (retries store once)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9–10</td><td>One event. <b>event_id</b> is for dedup; <b>occurred_at</b> is event time</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12–13</td><td><b>key=order ID</b> routes one order to one partition</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">14</td><td>Wait until everything is sent</td></tr></table></div><p class=\"g-small\">Consumer</p><pre><code> 1  from confluent_kafka import Consumer\n 2  import json\n 3  \n 4  consumer = Consumer({\n 5      \"bootstrap.servers\": \"localhost:9092\",\n 6      \"group.id\": \"sales-dashboard\",\n 7      \"auto.offset.reset\": \"earliest\",\n 8      \"enable.auto.commit\": False,\n 9  })\n10  consumer.subscribe([\"order-events\"])\n11  \n12  seen = set()\n13  while True:\n14      msg = consumer.poll(1.0)\n15      if msg is None or msg.error():\n16          continue\n17      event = json.loads(msg.value())\n18      if event[\"event_id\"] not in seen:\n19          seen.add(event[\"event_id\"])\n20          print(\"sales +\", event[\"amount\"])\n21      consumer.commit(msg)</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–9</td><td><b>group.id</b> is the team name; <b>earliest</b> starts from the beginning with no bookmark</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td><b>Auto-commit off</b> — commit manually, only after processing</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12–20</td><td>Poll every second; skip seen event_ids (in production keep this in a DB or Flink state, not memory)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">21</td><td>Commit only after processing</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.7 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why does adding consumers beyond the partition count not help?</summary><div>A partition goes to one consumer in a group at a time; extra consumers sit idle.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why key by order ID, and what is the cost?</summary><div>To preserve per-order ordering. The cost is that a hot key can make one partition a bottleneck.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>What goes wrong if you commit before processing?</summary><div>If you crash mid-processing the event is recorded as read and never returns → loss.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>2.8 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Replication factor and ISR tuning <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>Security such as SASL and ACLs <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>Compacted topics <span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">Concept only</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "contract", "title": "The Event Contract", "sub": "Ch. 3", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-contract\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">03</span>The Event Contract — Rules for Changing Shape</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>An event contract is the agreement between sender and receiver on which fields exist, what they mean and how they are typed, and how the shape may change.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>If a sender renames one field, the receiver reads an empty value without error and the sum quietly goes wrong.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.1 A minimal contract</h4><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"event_id\": \"e-001\",\n 3    \"event_type\": \"ORDER_CREATED\",\n 4    \"aggregate_id\": \"A-1001\",\n 5    \"occurred_at\": \"2026-10-14T10:01:00+09:00\",\n 6    \"schema_version\": 1,\n 7    \"payload\": { \"amount\": 42000, \"currency\": \"KRW\", \"status\": \"CREATED\" }\n 8  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td><b>event_id</b> — globally unique; the dedup key</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td><b>aggregate_id</b> — the business object (order); used as the Kafka key</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td><b>occurred_at</b> — when it happened (event time), with timezone</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td><b>schema_version</b> — lets readers branch when the shape changes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td><b>payload</b> — business content; always state unit and currency</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.2 Three kinds of compatibility</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Deploy first</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">backward</td><td>New readers can read old events</td><td>Consumers</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">forward</td><td>Old readers can read new events</td><td>Producers</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">full</td><td>Both</td><td>Any order</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.3 Change verdicts</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Change</th><th>Safe?</th><th>Why</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Add optional field with default</td><td>Safe</td><td>Old readers ignore it; new readers fall back to the default</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Add required field, no default</td><td>Risky</td><td>No value to fill when reading old events</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Remove a field</td><td>Conditional</td><td>Breaks old readers that require it</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Change a type</td><td>Usually risky</td><td>int→string fails; only widening (int→long) is sometimes allowed</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Rename</td><td>Risky</td><td>Looks like remove + add; needs aliases or a migration window</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">What compatibility checks cannot catch</b>Changing “won” to “thousand won” keeps the type and passes every check. Pin meaning down as units in the contract.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.4 A safe rename procedure</h4><ol><li><b>Add</b> the new field; the sender writes both old and new</li><li>Switch readers to the new field</li><li>Confirm nothing reads the old field</li><li>Stop writing the old field and remove it from the contract</li></ol></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.5 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why is adding a required field risky?</summary><div>Old events already stored have no value for it, so readers using the new shape cannot fill it.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why is a rename “remove + add”?</summary><div>Tools identify fields by name, so the old name disappears and a new one appears.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>3.6 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Avro/Protobuf syntax details <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>Registry operations and permissions <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "time", "title": "Time and Windows", "sub": "Ch. 4", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-time\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">04</span>Time and Windows — Aggregating by “When”</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>Event time is when something actually happened; processing time is when the system saw it. A watermark declares “events before this time have mostly arrived”, and a window cuts time into buckets.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Aggregating by arrival time drops a late-sent order into the wrong bucket, so the same data yields different numbers in different reports.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.1 How it works</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 214\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Event time vs arrival time\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"52\" class=\"g-ts2\">Happened</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"150\" class=\"g-ts2\">Arrived</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"60\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"150\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:00</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"194\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:02</text><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"194\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"194\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:04</text><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"442\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:06</text><line x1=\"442\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"442\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"442\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"442\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"566\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:08</text><line x1=\"566\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"566\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"566\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"566\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><text x=\"690\" y=\"200\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">10:10</text><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"56\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"64\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"690\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"690\" y2=\"154\" class=\"g-fl\"/><line x1=\"318\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"184\" class=\"g-flh g-fd\"/><text x=\"322\" y=\"26\" class=\"g-th\" style=\"font-size:12px\">Window edge 10:05</text><path d=\"M142,60 L143,150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><circle cx=\"143\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><path d=\"M370,60 L371,150\" class=\"g-fl\"/><circle cx=\"370\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><circle cx=\"371\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-fa\"/><path d=\"M375,60 L463,150\" class=\"g-flh\"/><circle cx=\"375\" cy=\"60\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-th\"/><circle cx=\"463\" cy=\"150\" r=\"6\" class=\"g-th\"/><text x=\"143\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">e1</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"46\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">e2 · e3</text><text x=\"470\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-th\" style=\"font-size:12px\">e3 · arrived 85 s late</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 4-1</b> e3 happened at 10:04:55 but arrived at 10:06:20; the window edge (10:05) sits in between.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Event</th><th>Happened</th><th>Arrived</th><th>Amount</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e1</td><td>10:01:10</td><td>10:01:11</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e2</td><td>10:04:50</td><td>10:04:51</td><td>20,000</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">e3</td><td>10:04:55</td><td>10:06:20</td><td>30,000</td></tr></table></div><p>Computing sales for the 10:00–10:05 bucket under each setting (assuming other orders keep arriving so the watermark advances):</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Bucket total</th><th>Finalized at</th><th>Reading</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Arrival time</td><td>30,000</td><td>10:05:00</td><td>e3 slips into the next bucket — wrong bucket</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Event time + 10 s watermark</td><td>30,000</td><td>10:05:10</td><td>e3 is late and dropped by default</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Event time + 120 s allowed lateness</td><td>60,000</td><td>10:07:00</td><td>Includes e3 but finalizes 2 minutes later</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Takeaway</b>How long to wait for late events is a <b>business decision</b>, not a technical one. It is a dial between accuracy and delay.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.2 Stage cards</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Choose the time basis</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">What counts as “the time”</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>The event’s occurred_at</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>The time field all aggregations use</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>The contract (Ch.3) and the Flink table</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Mixed timezones put events 9 hours off (UTC vs KST)</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Set the watermark</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">How late is still acceptable</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Measured delay distribution</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>An allowed delay (e.g., 10 s)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Business owner + data engineer</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Too short drops legitimate late data; too long delays results</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Handle late events</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Drop, wait, or divert</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Events arriving after the watermark</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Drop / allowed lateness / side output</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Flink job design</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Silent drops make totals fall short — at least count them</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ Pick a window type</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">The shape of the bucket</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>The question (per-minute sales? last 5 minutes? one visit?)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>tumbling / sliding / session</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Requirements</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Sliding puts one event in several buckets, increasing cost</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.3 Window types</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Type</th><th>Shape</th><th>Example</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">tumbling</td><td>Fixed, non-overlapping</td><td>Sales per minute</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">sliding</td><td>Overlapping, moving</td><td>5-minute moving average, refreshed each minute</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">session</td><td>Closes after a gap in activity</td><td>One customer’s visit</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.4 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Result never appears</td><td>An idle partition stalls the watermark</td><td>Set an idle timeout</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Totals short at night</td><td>Late events silently dropped</td><td>Monitor a late-event counter</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Devices disagree on time</td><td>Client clock skew</td><td>Also record server receive time</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Off by 9 hours</td><td>UTC/KST mixing</td><td>Fix a timezone-aware format in the contract</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.5 Code <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">Advanced</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">Flink SQL</p><pre><code> 1  CREATE TABLE orders (\n 2    order_id    STRING,\n 3    amount      DECIMAL(12, 0),\n 4    occurred_at TIMESTAMP(3),\n 5    WATERMARK FOR occurred_at AS occurred_at - INTERVAL '10' SECOND\n 6  ) WITH (\n 7    'connector' = 'kafka',\n 8    'topic' = 'order-events',\n 9    'properties.bootstrap.servers' = 'kafka:9092',\n10    'format' = 'json',\n11    'scan.startup.mode' = 'earliest-offset'\n12  );\n13  \n14  SELECT window_start, window_end, SUM(amount) AS sales\n15  FROM TABLE(\n16    TUMBLE(TABLE orders, DESCRIPTOR(occurred_at), INTERVAL '5' MINUTE))\n17  GROUP BY window_start, window_end;</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1–5</td><td>Declare the Kafka topic as an ever-growing table; <b>WATERMARK</b> means “wait up to 10 s”</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6–12</td><td>The source is the order-events topic, read from the start</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">14–17</td><td><b>TUMBLE</b> — cut into non-overlapping 5-minute buckets by occurred_at (event time)</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.6 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>What do you gain and lose by lengthening the watermark?</summary><div>You accept more late events (more accurate) but results finalize later.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why aggregate by event time instead of processing time?</summary><div>Because the same data produces the same result despite network delay or retries (reproducibility).</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>4.7 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Window joins and CEP <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>Flink DataStream API details <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "state", "title": "State and Recovery", "sub": "Ch. 5", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-state\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">05</span>State and Recovery — Why Numbers Survive a Crash</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>State is what a streaming job remembers mid-computation (totals, seen IDs); a checkpoint saves that state together with the read position at regular intervals.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Every crash wipes the totals or forces a full recompute — and re-reading can add the same event twice.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.1 How it works</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 144\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Checkpoint and recovery\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Read</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Kafka offset</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Update state</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">sum += amount</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Checkpoint</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">every 30 s</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Failure</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">server dies</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Restore</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">last snapshot</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Replay</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">since snapshot</text><path d=\"M666,90 C666,132 54,132 54,92\" class=\"g-fla g-fd\" marker-end=\"url(#g-aha)\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">resume reading from the saved offset</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 5-1</b> Because state and read position are saved <b>together</b>, a restore leaves the total and the position consistent.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Time (example)</th><th>Event</th><th>Total</th><th>Read position (P0)</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:00</td><td>Checkpoint cp-7 saved</td><td>1,250,000</td><td>900</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:20</td><td>Processing continues</td><td>1,310,000</td><td>940</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:25</td><td>Server dies</td><td>(memory lost)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:40</td><td>Restore from cp-7</td><td>1,250,000</td><td>900</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10:00:41~</td><td>Re-read 40 events (900–940) and recompute</td><td>1,310,000</td><td>940</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Reading it</b>The 40 events are re-read, yet nothing is added twice — the job restarts from the restored total (1,250,000).</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.2 What “exactly-once” really means</h4><p>Flink’s exactly-once does not mean each event is physically processed once; it means the result in <b>Flink-managed state</b> is applied once even after recovery. Writing to an external store exactly once needs more conditions.</p><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Source</th><th>Sink</th><th>End-to-end result</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Replayable (Kafka)</td><td>Transactional or idempotent</td><td>Applied exactly once</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Replayable</td><td>Plain INSERT</td><td>Recovered span may be written twice (duplicates)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Not replayable</td><td>Anything</td><td>May lose data</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.3 Checkpoint vs. savepoint</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Checkpoint</th><th>Savepoint</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Purpose</td><td>Automatic failure recovery</td><td>Upgrade, migration, rollback</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Created by</td><td>The system, periodically</td><td>A person, explicitly</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Lifetime</td><td>Managed by the system (old ones deleted)</td><td>Kept until you delete it</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.4 Stage cards — handling one failure</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Save</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Periodically save state + position together</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Operator state, source offsets</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A checkpoint file</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Flink</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Repeated failures leave an ever-older restore point → alert on it</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Detect</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Notice a worker is gone</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Missed heartbeats</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A decision to stop and restart</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Flink + Kubernetes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>If restarts loop, fix the cause (code/config) first</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Restore</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Rebuild state from the last good checkpoint</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Checkpoint location</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Totals and read position restored</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Flink</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>If a code change alters state shape, restore fails → verify with a savepoint</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ Replay and verify</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Re-read since the snapshot and reconcile numbers</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Events after the offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Same totals and unique counts before and after</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Operator</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>A non-idempotent sink duplicates the recovered span</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.5 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Doubled total after recovery</td><td>Non-idempotent sink</td><td>Primary-key upsert or transactional sink</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">State keeps growing</td><td>Dedup IDs kept forever</td><td>Set a state TTL</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Frequent checkpoint failures</td><td>Slow sink or state causes timeouts</td><td>Watch checkpoint duration</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Restore fails after deploy</td><td>Incompatible state shape</td><td>Pre-validate with a savepoint</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.6 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why save state and read position together?</summary><div>Saved separately, they diverge after restore, causing misses or double counts.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why can duplicates appear in the DB despite exactly-once?</summary><div>The guarantee covers Flink state; a non-idempotent, non-transactional sink applies the retry twice.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>5.7 Not covered</h4><ul><li>State backend (RocksDB) tuning <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>High-availability setup <span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">Concept only</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "cdc", "title": "CDC and Outbox", "sub": "Ch. 6", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-cdc\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">06</span>CDC and Outbox — Turning DB Changes into Events Without Gaps</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>CDC reads the change log a database already writes and emits row changes as events. Outbox is a pattern that stores business data and an “event to publish” record in one transaction.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>If an app writes to the DB and Kafka separately, there is a moment when only one succeeds — and the missing order is never reconciled.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.1 How it works <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">Advanced</span></h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 190\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Dual write vs CDC\"><text x=\"10\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-t\">Dual write (risky)</text><rect x=\"10\" y=\"34\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">Order app</text><path d=\"M112,50 L200,40\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><path d=\"M112,68 L200,108\" class=\"g-flh\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"202\" y=\"24\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">DB saved ✔</text><rect x=\"202\" y=\"92\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka failed ✘</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Order in DB, missing from Kafka</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"20\" class=\"g-t\">CDC / outbox (safe)</text><rect x=\"400\" y=\"34\" width=\"100\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"450\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">Order app</text><path d=\"M502,59 L528,59\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"530\" y=\"34\" width=\"90\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"575\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">DB</text><text x=\"575\" y=\"71\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:12px\">+ outbox</text><path d=\"M622,59 L648,59\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"650\" y=\"34\" width=\"62\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"681\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">CDC</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"112\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Business row + publish intent in one transaction</text><text x=\"560\" y=\"130\" class=\"g-ts2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">CDC reads only committed rows → Kafka</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 6-1</b> Dual writes have a gap between two systems; CDC/outbox follows only what the DB has committed.</figcaption></figure><p>A database writes every change to a log first (PostgreSQL’s WAL). A CDC tool such as Debezium reads it and emits events like “order A-1001 went from CREATED to PAID”.</p><p class=\"g-small\">A Debezium change event (example)</p><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"op\": \"u\",\n 3    \"before\": { \"id\": \"A-1001\", \"status\": \"CREATED\", \"amount\": 42000 },\n 4    \"after\":  { \"id\": \"A-1001\", \"status\": \"PAID\",    \"amount\": 42000 },\n 5    \"source\": { \"lsn\": 33100248, \"ts_ms\": 1760403667000 }\n 6  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">2</td><td><b>op</b> — c create, u update, d delete, r initial snapshot</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3–4</td><td><b>before/after</b> — the row before and after, so you can diff</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5</td><td><b>lsn</b> — log position; use it to drop a repeated change</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.2 Stage cards</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Initial snapshot</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Emit all existing rows first</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Current rows of the target tables</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A batch of op=r events</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Debezium</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Large tables take long and load the DB → schedule off-peak</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Switch to streaming</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Follow changes made after the snapshot</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>The log position at snapshot time</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>op=c/u/d events</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Debezium</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>The same row may arrive twice around the switch → dedupe</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Resume after failure</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Re-read from the saved log position</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Last offset (LSN)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Events after the break</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Kafka Connect</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>A replication slot keeps WAL and can fill the DB disk</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ Schema change</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">When a column is added or dropped</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>A DDL change</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Events in the new shape</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>DBA + the Ch.3 contract</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Readers unaware of the new column ignore or fail — follow the compatibility rules</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.3 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">DB disk keeps filling</td><td>Replication slot pins WAL (connector down)</td><td>Monitor slot lag; drop unused slots</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Deletes not reflected</td><td>Consumer ignores op=d</td><td>State the delete policy in the contract</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Same change twice</td><td>CDC is at-least-once</td><td>Dedupe by key + lsn</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Latency spike on big transactions</td><td>Events release only on commit</td><td>Commit bulk changes in chunks</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.4 Code — connector config <span class=\"g-badge g-b-fill\">Advanced</span></h4><p class=\"g-small\">Debezium config</p><pre><code> 1  {\n 2    \"name\": \"shop-orders-cdc\",\n 3    \"config\": {\n 4      \"connector.class\": \"io.debezium.connector.postgresql.PostgresConnector\",\n 5      \"database.hostname\": \"postgres\",\n 6      \"database.dbname\": \"shop\",\n 7      \"database.user\": \"cdc_reader\",\n 8      \"database.password\": \"${file:/secrets/cdc.properties:password}\",\n 9      \"plugin.name\": \"pgoutput\",\n10      \"topic.prefix\": \"shop\",\n11      \"table.include.list\": \"public.orders,public.payments\"\n12    }\n13  }</code></pre><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Line</th><th>What it does</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4</td><td>The PostgreSQL CDC connector</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">5–7</td><td>Which DB to watch; use a read-only account</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td>Never hard-code the password; read it from a secret store</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9</td><td>PostgreSQL’s built-in decoding plugin</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">10–11</td><td><b>topic.prefix</b> prefixes topic names; <b>table.include.list</b> lists tables to follow</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.5 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why is CDC safer than dual writes?</summary><div>It reads only committed changes, shrinking the “in DB, not in Kafka” gap; with an outbox, the publish intent joins the same transaction.</div></details><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Why can CDC events repeat?</summary><div>After a restart it re-reads from the last saved position (at-least-once).</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>6.6 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Databases other than PostgreSQL <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li><li>Standalone Debezium Server <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "store", "title": "Storage and Query", "sub": "Ch. 7", "part": "Core", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-store\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">07</span>Storage and Query — Keeping “Now” and “Back Then” Apart</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>A real-time analytical store (such as StarRocks) answers “current state and recent aggregates” fast; a table-format store (Iceberg) keeps “every change” cheaply for long and enables recomputation as of any past time.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Try to do everything in one and queries are slow — or you have no source to repair a wrong number.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.1 The question picks the store</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 126\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Splitting storage roles\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"115\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">Flink</text><text x=\"115\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Processed output</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"360\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Current state</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">fast queries</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"219\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"605\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\">Dashboard / API</text><text x=\"605\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">second-level reads</text><text x=\"360\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">Flink also writes to Iceberg. If numbers go wrong, recompute from Iceberg and overwrite StarRocks.</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 7-1</b> One computed result, stored in two places</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Question</th><th>Right place</th><th>Why</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">What is order A-1001’s status now?</td><td>StarRocks</td><td>Latest value by key (upsert)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">The dashboard must load in 1 s</td><td>StarRocks</td><td>Columnar storage, parallel execution</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">What were orders like yesterday at 2 pm?</td><td>Iceberg</td><td>Snapshots allow time-travel reads</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Recompute last month with a new rule</td><td>Iceberg</td><td>The full history is retained</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.2 Comparison</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>StarRocks</th><th>Iceberg</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Role</td><td>A fast query database</td><td>A storage (table) format</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Strength</td><td>Low-latency aggregation and reads</td><td>History, snapshots, multi-engine reads</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Weakness</td><td>Cost grows if you keep all history</td><td>Too slow for second-level dashboards</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Ops note</td><td>Key/partition design drives performance</td><td>Small files pile up; compaction needed</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.3 Stage cards</h4><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Load</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Write the same result to both</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Flink output (with primary key)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>StarRocks rows, Iceberg snapshots</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Flink connectors</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>One-sided success splits the numbers → reconcile in ②</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Reconcile</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Compare counts and sums across both</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Both stores’ values for one range</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Zero diff, or a diff report</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Operator / automated check</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>On mismatch, treat Iceberg as the source of truth</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Recompute</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Recompute from the source and overwrite</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Iceberg history, the corrected rule</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>New results in StarRocks</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Data engineer</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Build into a new table and swap, so reads never mix old and new</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.4 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">One order in two rows</td><td>Wrong primary key</td><td>Key on the business ID</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Iceberg reads slow down</td><td>Small files accumulate</td><td>Schedule compaction</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Stores disagree</td><td>One load lagged or failed</td><td>Automate the ② reconciliation</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.5 Check yourself</h4><details class=\"g-qa\"><summary>Where do you ask for “now” vs. “yesterday at 2 pm”?</summary><div>Now → StarRocks; yesterday 2 pm → an Iceberg snapshot.</div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>7.6 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Comparison with other analytical DBs (e.g., ClickHouse) <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">Depends</span></li><li>Catalog and access control <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "ops", "title": "Operations", "sub": "Ch. 8", "part": "Operations", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-ops\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">08</span>Operations — More Than a “Success” Log</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>Operational standards commit you to continuously verifying “the numbers are right and on time”, not merely “the program is running”.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>The job logs success while totals are wrong or six hours late — and users find out first.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.1 What to watch</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Metric</th><th>Warning sign</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Kafka</td><td>Consumer lag, throughput</td><td>Lag keeps rising; one partition skewed</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink</td><td>Backpressure, checkpoint duration/failures, restarts</td><td>Consecutive checkpoint failures, restart loops</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Data</td><td>In/out counts, unique keys, amount sums, null rate, DLQ</td><td>System healthy but business numbers differ</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Store</td><td>Commit latency, rejected rows, freshness</td><td>Falling success rate, stale latest time</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">User</td><td>Latest data timestamp shown on screen</td><td>Pipeline fine, yet reads are stale</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.2 Example targets (SLOs)</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Learning target</th><th>How to verify</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">End-to-end latency p95</td><td>≤ 10 s</td><td>occurred_at vs. time visible in queries</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Loss</td><td>0</td><td>Compare source event_ids with Iceberg</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Business duplicates</td><td>0</td><td>Send one event_id three times; amount counted once</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Recovery time</td><td>≤ 5 min</td><td>From killing a worker to throughput recovery</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.3 Incident response</h4><details class=\"g-stage\" open><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">① Narrow the impact</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Which screens and time spans are wrong</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>User reports, alerts</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Affected consumers and time range</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>On-call</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Unknown scope means over- or under-recovery</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">② Follow the flow to the bottleneck</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Source → Kafka lag → Flink backpressure → sink</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Per-layer metrics (8.1)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>The blocked point</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>On-call</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Adding consumers often does not help (partition cap, slow sink)</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">③ Judge consistency</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Loss/duplicate risk and whether auto-restart is safe</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Count and sum checks</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>“Safe to restart” or “stop and recover”</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>On-call + business owner</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>If wrong numbers keep flowing, stop publishing first</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">④ Recover and verify</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Restore from a safe point and reconcile</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Last safe checkpoint/savepoint, offset</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>Both system metrics and business numbers are healthy</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>On-call</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>Never stop at system metrics alone</td></tr></table></div></div></details><details class=\"g-stage\"><summary><span class=\"g-stage-t\">⑤ Prevent recurrence</span><span class=\"g-stage-s\">Turn the warning into an automated check</span></summary><div class=\"g-stage-b\"><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Input</td><td>Post-incident notes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Output</td><td>A new alert, guard, or test</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Owner</td><td>Team</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">If it fails</td><td>“Let’s be careful” guarantees repeats</td></tr></table></div></div></details></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.4 Deploy and rollback checklist</h4><ul class=\"g-checklist\"><li>CI checks the input contract for breaking changes</li><li>Record the savepoint to roll back to</li><li>Confirm old and new versions may run at the same time</li><li>Validate on a slice of real input via a separate consumer group</li><li>Compare counts, sums, and latest time with the old version</li><li>Write down the rollback command and the replay start offset</li></ul></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.5 Failure cases</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Prevention</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Alert fatigue</td><td>Every metric alerts with no threshold</td><td>Page only on user-impact metrics</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Success logs but wrong numbers</td><td>No business-level checks</td><td>Make count/sum reconciliation a metric</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>8.6 Not covered</h4><ul><li>On-call rotation design <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">Depends</span></li><li>Cost optimization <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "build", "title": "Build It", "sub": "Ch. 9", "part": "Practice", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-build\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">09</span>Build It — A Fake Order-and-Payment Pipeline</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>The capstone runs every chapter on fake order and payment data so you can confirm each claim with numbers.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Reading alone leaves a gap between “I understand” and “I can build it”.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.1 What you will build</h4><figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 720 104\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Capstone architecture\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"54\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Postgres</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"58\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">orders</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">payments</text><path d=\"M104,51 L126,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"128\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fw\"/><text x=\"176\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Debezium</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">CDC</text><path d=\"M227,51 L249,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"251\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fo\"/><text x=\"299\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Kafka</text><text x=\"299\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">contract check</text><path d=\"M349,51 L371,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"373\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fb\"/><text x=\"421\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Flink</text><text x=\"421\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">join, dedupe</text><path d=\"M471,51 L493,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"495\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fas\"/><text x=\"544\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">StarRocks</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Iceberg</text><text x=\"544\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">now / history</text><path d=\"M594,51 L616,51\" class=\"g-fl\" marker-end=\"url(#g-ah)\"/><rect x=\"618\" y=\"14\" width=\"96\" height=\"74\" rx=\"8\" class=\"g-fh\"/><text x=\"666\" y=\"47\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-t\" style=\"font-size:13px\">Observe</text><text x=\"666\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"g-ts2\">lag·DLQ</text></svg><figcaption><b>Figure 9-1</b> Order and payment changes appear on the dashboard within 10 s, and amounts are not duplicated across failures and restarts</figcaption></figure><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Success criterion</th><th>Target</th><th>Check</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">End-to-end p95</td><td>≤ 10s</td><td>occurred_at vs visible time</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Loss</td><td>0</td><td>Source vs. Iceberg counts</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Duplicates</td><td>0</td><td>Publish one event_id three times</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Recovery</td><td>≤ 5 min</td><td>Kill-a-worker experiment</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Contract safety</td><td>Block 100% of breaking changes</td><td>Compatibility test in CI</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Reuse</td><td>A second pipeline needs config only</td><td>Create a shipment pipeline</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Safety rules</b>Practice only on your own machine (docker compose) with fake data — never company servers or real data.</div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.2 12-week roadmap</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Week</th><th>Topic</th><th>Done when</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">0</td><td>Baseline: sketch the architecture</td><td>Draft in 20 min; ≤ 10 unknowns</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">1–2</td><td>Kafka: topics, partitions, keys, groups (Ch.2)</td><td>Replay by changing offsets; explain ordering scope from logs</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">3</td><td>Event contract (Ch.3)</td><td>CI tells compatible from breaking changes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">4–5</td><td>Flink SQL, event time, watermarks (Ch.4)</td><td>Prove the difference between the two bases on the same input</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">6</td><td>State, checkpoints, restarts (Ch.5)</td><td>Same unique count and sum before and after</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">7</td><td>Postgres CDC (Ch.6)</td><td>Complete ordered history; delete policy documented</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">8</td><td>Connect the stores (Ch.7)</td><td>Answer “now” and “as of yesterday” from the right stores</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">9–10</td><td>Kubernetes ops, observability, SLOs (Ch.8)</td><td>Evidence of how fast an alert fires after a sink outage</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">11</td><td>Config-driven standardization</td><td>Generate a second pipeline without copying code</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">12</td><td>Capstone review</td><td>Answer 12+ questions below with diagrams and measurements</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.3 Skill levels</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Level</th><th>Criterion</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Can explain</td><td>Explain the check questions without notes</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Can build</td><td>Rebuild the happy path from scratch</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Can operate</td><td>Recover six failure experiments and reconcile numbers</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Can platformize</td><td>Second pipeline from config and SQL only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Can lead</td><td>Ask for SLOs, contracts, keys, guarantees, stores, rollback up front</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>9.4 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Real data and real servers <span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">Depends</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "vibe", "title": "Instructing an AI", "sub": "Ch. 10", "part": "Advanced", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-vibe\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">10</span>Instructing an AI — Known Terms Mean Less Wandering</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>Vibe coding means directing an AI in plain language; the keywords here are constraints that make the AI write code that does not go wrong, not just a demo that runs.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Without constraints an AI returns the most common example — which protects against none of duplicates, loss, or reordering.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.1 Keyword dictionary</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Keyword</th><th>Meaning</th><th>What changes</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">partition key = order_id</td><td>One order, one lane</td><td>Avoids order-scrambling code</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">idempotent producer / event_id dedup</td><td>Duplicate protection</td><td>Retries do not double-count</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">manual offset commit after processing</td><td>Bookmark after work</td><td>A loss-free consume loop</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">event time + watermark (10s)</td><td>Aggregate by event time</td><td>Late data not silently skipped</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">tumbling window 1 minute</td><td>One-minute buckets</td><td>Exact aggregation unit</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">checkpoint / exactly-once sink</td><td>Save points, apply once</td><td>Numbers survive restarts</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">DLQ (dead letter queue)</td><td>A bin for broken events</td><td>Collects instead of dropping</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">schema registry, backward compatible</td><td>Shape agreement</td><td>Protects readers on change</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">docker compose, local only, fake data</td><td>Local, fake data</td><td>Never touches company servers</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.2 Same request, different result</h4><div class=\"g-grid2\"><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Prompt that wanders</b><br>Write code to stream orders through Kafka</div><div class=\"g-key g-okkey\"><b class=\"g-l\">Prompt that stays on track</b><br>Write an order-events producer with Python confluent-kafka: key=order_id, idempotent producer on, events carry event_id and occurred_at (ISO 8601). The consumer uses group.id=sales-dashboard, manual offset commit after processing, and event_id dedup. Include a docker compose with one local Kafka and a test using 100 fake orders.</div></div><p class=\"g-small\">Why it differs: Fixing the key, dedup, and bookmark rules up front steers the AI away from “runs for now” toward “does not go wrong”.</p><div class=\"g-grid2\"><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Prompt that wanders</b><br>Aggregate sales per minute with Flink</div><div class=\"g-key g-okkey\"><b class=\"g-l\">Prompt that stays on track</b><br>With Flink SQL, read Kafka order-events and sum sales in 1-minute tumbling windows by occurred_at, with a 10 s watermark. Send malformed rows to a DLQ topic, print results to the console, and comment why event time rather than processing time is used.</div></div><p class=\"g-small\">Why it differs: If you do not name the time basis, the AI usually uses processing time, dropping late orders.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.3 A prompt template</h4><ol><li><b>What</b>: a one-line goal (e.g., per-minute sales)</li><li><b>Input/output</b>: topic names and event fields</li><li><b>Guarantees</b>: no duplicates / no loss / ordering scope</li><li><b>Time</b>: the basis (event time) and allowed lateness</li><li><b>Environment</b>: local, docker compose, fake data</li><li><b>Verification</b>: which experiment proves it (e.g., same event three times)</li></ol></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.4 Review AI-written code</h4><ul class=\"g-checklist\"><li>Is the key a business ID such as order ID?</li><li>Is the offset commit <b>after</b> processing?</li><li>Is there an event_id for dedup?</li><li>Is aggregation by event time?</li><li>Are passwords hard-coded?</li><li>Is the practice local with fake data?</li></ul></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>10.5 Not covered</h4><ul><li>Tool-specific usage of any AI product <span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></li></ul></section></div>"}, {"id": "limits", "title": "Out of Scope and Choices", "sub": "Ch. 11", "part": "Boundaries", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-limits\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">11</span>Out of Scope and Choices</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>This chapter gathers, openly, what the book deliberately leaves out and the choices whose answers depend on context.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Hidden boundaries read as “not in the book, so unnecessary” — and the first things omitted in production are exactly these.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>11.1 Not covered</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Topic</th><th>Status</th><th>Where to look</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Security (auth, encryption, access)</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></td><td>Each product’s security docs</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Cost estimation</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></td><td>Cloud pricing calculators</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Multi-region and DR</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-warn\">Concept only</span></td><td>Kafka and Flink HA docs</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Privacy and compliance</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></td><td>Your privacy/compliance owner</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Alternatives such as Kafka Streams and ksqlDB</td><td><span class=\"g-badge g-b-neutral\">Not covered</span></td><td>Official docs</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>11.2 Undecided — it depends</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Question</th><th>Decision criteria</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Self-host vs. managed</td><td>Staffing, incident ownership, cost (<span class=\"g-badge g-b-danger\">Depends</span>)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Flink vs. plain consumer code</td><td>Do you need state, time, joins? Otherwise a simple consumer may do</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">Do you really need real-time?</td><td>Does lateness cost you? Otherwise batch is enough (Ch.1)</td></tr></table></div></section></div>"}, {"id": "ref", "title": "Glossary, Sources, Revisions", "sub": "Ch. 12", "part": "Appendix", "html": "<div class=\"g-chapter\" id=\"g-pl-ref\"><h3><span class=\"g-cn\">12</span>Glossary · Sources · Revisions</h3><div class=\"g-key\"><b class=\"g-l\">Definition</b>This chapter collects every term in Korean and English, and records the sources behind technical claims and the document’s revision history.</div><div class=\"g-trap\"><b class=\"g-l\">Without it</b>Scattered terms get understood differently per chapter; without sources, errors have nowhere to be corrected.</div><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.1 Glossary</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-event\">Event</span></td><td>A one-line record of “what happened, when”</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-topic\">Topic</span></td><td>A named stream where events of one kind are kept</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-partition\">Partition</span></td><td>One lane of a topic; ordering is guaranteed only inside it</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-key\">Key</span></td><td>A value that routes equal keys to the same partition</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-offset\">Offset</span></td><td>Position within a partition; the reader’s bookmark</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-group\">Consumer group</span></td><td>Consumers sharing one job</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-idem\">Idempotence</span></td><td>Repeating a request has the same effect as doing it once</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-et\">Event time</span></td><td>When the event actually happened</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-pt\">Processing time</span></td><td>When the system saw it</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-wm\">Watermark</span></td><td>A line saying “events before this time have mostly arrived”</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-window\">Window</span></td><td>A way to cut time into buckets</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-state\">State</span></td><td>Values a streaming job remembers (totals, etc.)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-cp\">Checkpoint</span></td><td>An automatic save of state plus read position</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-sp\">Savepoint</span></td><td>A manual save for upgrades and rollbacks</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-cdc\">CDC</span></td><td>Reading a DB change log and turning it into events</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-outbox\">Outbox</span></td><td>Saving the business row and publish intent in one transaction</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-dlq\">DLQ</span></td><td>A place to collect events that could not be processed</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-slo\">SLO</span></td><td>A service-level target to keep (e.g., latency ≤ 10 s)</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-lag\">Consumer lag</span></td><td>Events written but not yet read</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\"><span id=\"g-pl-term-bp\">Backpressure</span></td><td>Upstream slowing down because downstream is slow</td></tr></table></div></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.2 Sources</h4><ol class=\"g-sources\"><li><a href=\"https://kafka.apache.org/quickstart/\">Apache Kafka Quickstart</a> — First run of topics, producers, consumers</li><li><a href=\"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/concepts/time/\">Flink — Event Time & Watermarks</a> — Event time and watermarks</li><li><a href=\"https://nightlies.apache.org/flink/flink-docs-stable/docs/learn-flink/fault_tolerance/\">Flink — Fault Tolerance</a> — Conditions for end-to-end exactly-once</li><li><a href=\"https://debezium.io/documentation/reference/stable/architecture.html\">Debezium — Architecture</a> — Kafka Connect–based CDC architecture</li><li><a href=\"https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/schema-registry/fundamentals/schema-evolution.html\">Schema Registry — Evolution</a> — Compatibility types</li><li><a href=\"https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/spark-getting-started/\">Apache Iceberg — Getting Started</a> — Tables and snapshots</li><li><a href=\"https://docs.starrocks.io/docs/loading/Flink-connector-starrocks/\">StarRocks — Flink connector</a> — Loading from Flink in real time</li></ol><p>Versions change; re-check the stable docs on the day you start. Exactly-once means once-applied to state; end-to-end guarantees need a replayable source plus an idempotent or transactional sink.</p></section><section class=\"g-topic\"><h4>12.3 Revision history</h4><div class=\"g-tw\"><table><tr><th>Version</th><th>Date</th><th>Change</th></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">v0.2</td><td>2026-10-15</td><td>Full rewrite into a fixed frame (definition, reason, mechanics, stage cards, failures, out-of-scope, glossary). Korean and English together.</td></tr><tr><td class=\"g-h\">v0.1</td><td>2026-10-14</td><td>First draft (concept-centered intro, Korean)</td></tr></table></div></section></div>"}];
